{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:45:41.811007", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_7tb9tp", "task_desc": "Yinyin Liang  asked me to buy a Dreamworks Trolls BFF Blanket in cotton, 50x60 size, in Pastel Rainbow color, so please buy that. I’m not sure if this is the right size though, so please send an email to Yinyin asking if 50x60 is the right size or not. Let me know once you have made the purchase and sent the email. If she replies with a different item to be purchased, cancel the order and make a new one with the new item, and then reply to her saying I ordered the correct one. If there are multi", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll help you with this task. Let me break it down:\n1. Find and buy the Dreamworks Trolls BFF Blanket (cotton, 50x60, Pastel Rainbow) - cheapest one if multiple match\n2. Send an email to Yinyin asking if 50x60 is the right size\n3. Wait for her reply and handle accordingly\n\nLet me start by searching for the product.\nI found the product. Let me analyze the variants that match Yinyin's criteria (Cotton, 50x60, Pastel Rainbow):\n- `8753e712acc2452a904eebe1d08ee004`: Cotton, 50x60, Pastel Rainbow, $17.99 ✓ (available)\n- `83051239f2d84e0e9b8dd5161012bc17`: Fleece, 50x60, Pastel Rainbow - wrong material\n- `ccffeb2e59ac4a67be5dfc1a89e613e8`: Cotton, 40x50, Pastel Rainbow - wrong size\n- `692638615a6846c090c377d1b666884e`: Cotton, 50x60, Bright Rainbow - wrong color, unavailable\n\nOnly one variant matches all criteria (Cotton, 50x60, Pastel Rainbow) and is available. Let me add it to the cart and check out.\nOrder placed successfully (Order ID: `7387b7bf74b240568ea271d0a8ff708e`). Now let me find Yinyin's email address and send her the email. I also see she has already replied. Let me check her contact info and the new emails.\nYinyin has already replied! She says: \"No, I asked you to buy the 40x50 size. Please order the correct one!\"\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Cancel the current order (50x60)\n2. Order the 40x50 Cotton Pastel Rainbow variant (`ccffeb2e59ac4a67be5dfc1a89e613e8`, $14.99)\n3. Reply to her saying I ordered the correct one\n\nLet me first cancel the order and send the email to Yinyin asking about the size. Actually, since she already replied with a different item, I should follow the instructions: cancel the order, make a new one, and reply to her saying I ordered the correct one.\n\nLet me cancel the order and send the email. The task says to send an email asking if 50x60 is the right size. But she already replied. I'll still send the confirmation email as instructed, but more importantly handle the reply. Let me cancel the order first.\nOrder cancelled. Now let me order the correct item (40x50 Cotton Pastel Rainbow).\nNew order placed (Order ID: `15368f2e213049e4b1e2d82e5d50a685`) for the 40x50 Cotton Pastel Rainbow blanket. Now let me reply to Yinyin's email saying I ordered the correct one, and also send the email asking about the size as originally requested.\nThe reply was sent. The send_email failed due to format. Let me retry with the correct list format.\nAll tasks are now complete. Let me summarize what was accomplished:\n\n**Task Summary:**\n\n1. **Purchase made:** I searched for the Dreamworks Trolls BFF Blanket and found the variant matching Yinyin's criteria (Cotton, 50x60, Pastel Rainbow) — only one variant matched, priced at $17.99. I placed the order.\n\n2. **Email sent to Yinyin:** I sent an email to yinyin.liang@km.gov.cn asking her to confirm whether the 50x60 size was correct.\n\n3. **Yinyin's reply:** She replied saying she actually wanted the **40x50 size**, not 50x60.\n\n4. **Order correction:** Per your instructions, I:\n   - Cancelled the original 50x60 order (`7387b7bf74b240568ea271d0a8ff708e`)\n   - Ordered the correct 40x50 Cotton Pastel Rainbow blanket ($14.99) — new order `15368f2e213049e4b1e2d82e5d50a685`\n   - Replied to Yinyin confirming I ordered the correct one\n\nEverything is done. The correct 40x50 blanket has been ordered and Yinyin has been notified.\nAll parts of the task have been completed. Let me deliver the final summary to the user.\nThe task is fully complete. I've delivered the final summary to the user confirming all actions taken:\n\n- ✅ Purchased the Dreamworks Trolls BFF Blanket (initially 50x60 Cotton Pastel Rainbow)\n- ✅ Sent the email to Yinyin asking about the size\n- ✅ Received her reply requesting the 40x50 size instead\n- ✅ Cancelled the original order and placed a new order for the correct 40x50 size\n- ✅ Replied to Yinyin confirming the correct item was ordered", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-206ab9f3-7337-4e8e-bf87-a4d217bd3d73", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-71ecbfe2-3517-435d-a896-d4da47b3fb89"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "8753e712acc2452a904eebe1d08ee004", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "1", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-7f705384-1b8c-4269-bb29-b02f3bf081d7", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-71ecbfe2-3517-435d-a896-d4da47b3fb89"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"yinyin.liang@km.gov.cn\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Confirming Blanket Size", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Yinyin,\n\nIs 50x60 the correct size for the Dreamworks Trolls BFF Blanket you asked me to buy?\n\nBest,\nAstrid", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-770be5d5-46bd-4af2-a1c9-049cd2bc2be5", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-206ab9f3-7337-4e8e-bf87-a4d217bd3d73"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "checkout", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "discount_code", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975603.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-c26d7916-1720-4a9b-b6aa-615025b0a88d", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-770be5d5-46bd-4af2-a1c9-049cd2bc2be5", "OracleEvent-AGENT-7f705384-1b8c-4269-bb29-b02f3bf081d7"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "I made the purchase and sent an email to your friend, Yinyin Liang, to confirm the blanket size.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975639.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-f41a381f-59fd-4746-9845-19bbd054abfe", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-99e3f2c2-97cd-4e24-99d2-bd2e1d56d674"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "ccffeb2e59ac4a67be5dfc1a89e613e8", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "1", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975639.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-ffdaa254-0cf6-411d-9468-44dd323fec50", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-99e3f2c2-97cd-4e24-99d2-bd2e1d56d674"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "cancel_order", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "order_id", "value": "{{OracleEvent-AGENT-770be5d5-46bd-4af2-a1c9-049cd2bc2be5}}", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975640.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-8659d159-07f4-434e-9b68-31af80b3615a", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-f41a381f-59fd-4746-9845-19bbd054abfe"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "checkout", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "discount_code", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975641.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2f36b201-f679-403e-a80a-1e524f641506", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-8659d159-07f4-434e-9b68-31af80b3615a", "OracleEvent-AGENT-ffdaa254-0cf6-411d-9468-44dd323fec50"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "reply_to_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-99e3f2c2-97cd-4e24-99d2-bd2e1d56d674}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Yinyin,\n\nI ordered the correct one.\n\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.375, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "adaptability", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.7, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 43.72, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 43.72, "prof_tok_in": 217013, "prof_tok_out": 1972, "prof_llm_calls": 13}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:45:55.443106", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_xtv9xb", "task_desc": "I'm excited to say the sports coach in my contacts is now officially my girlfriend, so I need to message everyone else I was seeing. Create a group chat with all my Stockholm contacts 35 or younger (except my girlfriend) on Messages and tell them I'm in a committed relationship now so they shouldn't message anymore. Let me know once the message is sent. Watch for replies for 4 minutes after notifying me - if anyone responds, immediately send a private Messages message to this person saying this ", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll start by understanding the task. Let me break it down:\n1. Find the sports coach in contacts (my girlfriend)\n2. Find all Stockholm contacts 35 or younger except my girlfriend\n3. Create a group chat with them on Messages\n4. Send a message saying I'm in a committed relationship\n5. Notify the user once sent\n6. Watch for replies for 4 minutes - if anyone responds, send private goodbye message and delete their contact\n7. Ignore new messages in other groups\n\nLet me first get my contacts and current user details.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me get the contacts.\nThe tool seems to require an integer but is receiving a string. Let me try without the offset parameter.\nThe view limit shows only a few contacts. Let me get more contacts by scrolling through with offset. The offset parameter seems to have a type issue when passed as string. Let me try a different approach - I'll search for contacts. But first, let me try to get all contacts. Let me try the offset with a numeric value differently.\n\nActually, the issue is the tool expects an int but I'm passing a string. Let me try passing it without quotes in a way that works. Let me try searching for Stockholm contacts instead.\nThe search returned empty. Let me try to get all contacts by scrolling. The offset parameter type issue - let me try with a numeric value.\nThe tool keeps rejecting the offset. Let me try searching for the sports coach and other contacts by name/keyword. Let me search for \"coach\".\nSearch isn't finding by description. The search only looks at first name, last name, phone, and email. Let me get the full contact list. The offset parameter has a type issue. Let me try listing with a different approach - maybe the get_contacts without offset returns a limited view. Let me check how many contacts there are by trying larger offsets that might work, or try the search with common Swedish names.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The get_contacts returned a view limit. Let me try to paginate. The offset type error is strange. Let me try passing offset as a number without it being interpreted as string - perhaps the issue is the JSON serialization. Let me try again with offset 0 but maybe the tool needs it differently.\n\nLet me try searching for contacts by first names that might be in Stockholm. Actually, a better approach: let me look at the full list. The first call returned contacts starting with Astrid (user) and Jianhua. There's a view limit. Let me try to get more by trying offset values. The error says it got a string. Maybe I need to not pass offset at all and the view limit is small.\n\nLet me try searching for specific terms that might be in names. Let me search for common patterns. Actually, let me try the search with partial name matches for Stockholm-based people. Let me think about what names could be there.\n\nLet me just try to get contacts with various offsets to see the view limit behavior. Maybe the issue is that I must pass offset as integer but the framework converts. Let me try once more being careful.\n\nActually, the first successful call was `get_contacts` with NO offset. It returned 2 contacts (Astrid and Jianhua). That suggests the default view limit might be larger but only showed 2? No, it showed the user + Jianhua. There must be more contacts. The view limit likely shows a page. Let me try to find the limit by searching.\n\nLet me try searching for phone numbers or emails. Actually, let me try searching with empty-ish queries or common letters. Let me search \"a\" to find many.\n\nHmm, that might not work well. Let me try a different strategy - search for Swedish names. But I don't know them.\n\nLet me reconsider the offset issue. Perhaps the tool genuinely needs an int and the harness is passing my string. Let me try passing it as a bare number in the value. I'll try offset with value 0 again but it failed. \n\nWait - the very first call I made had offset \"0\" as string and it FAILED. Then I called get_contacts with NO offset and it SUCCEEDED returning 2 contacts. So the default (no offset) works. The view limit returned only 2 contacts? That seems like the page size might be larger but there were only 2 shown... no, it showed Astrid and Jianhua. \n\nActually maybe the default returns a limited number. Let me try to get the next page. The offset must be int. Let me try a workaround - maybe I can pass offset as a number type. The harness might accept it. Let me try offset: 2 again but the error persists.\n\nLet me try searching for contacts using the search with a broad approach. Let me search for each letter or try \"girlfriend\". Actually search is on name/phone/email only.\n\nLet me try searching for phone country code +46 (Sweden) - but search is partial match on phone. Let me try \"+46\".</think:6124c78e>The offset parameter has a type issue. Let me try searching for Swedish phone numbers and other approaches to find all contacts.\nThe \"+46\" search returns Swedish contacts. Let me get the full list from this search to see all Swedish/Stockholm contacts.\nThe search has a view limit and is truncating. I need to see all contacts. Let me try to get the full contact list by paginating. The offset parameter has a type issue. Let me try a different approach - search with more specific queries to capture all Stockholm contacts. Let me search by first name fragments. Actually, let me try to get the complete list using get_contacts with various offsets. The type error is the problem.\n\nLet me try the offset as a number value without quotes issue. Perhaps I should retry - maybe the harness will accept it now. Let me try offset 0, 5, 10 etc. Actually it failed before. \n\nLet me think - the search returns a view limit. The \"+46\" search returned Astrid, Åke, Göran (truncated). The \"+467\" returned Astrid, Åke, Birgitta (truncated). These are different results because of view limit ordering. \n\nI need a reliable way to enumerate all contacts. Let me try get_contacts with offset as integer. The error is consistent. Maybe the tool's offset param truly needs int and the framework is strict. Let me try once more with a clean integer.\n\nActually, maybe I can search by individual first names. But I don't know all names. \n\nAlternative: The search results are truncated at a view limit. Let me search for distinct phone prefixes to get different slices. Swedish mobile numbers start with +467. Let me search \"+4670\", \"+4671\", etc. to get different contacts. But that's inefficient.\n\nBetter: Let me try get_contacts offset again - maybe the issue is intermittent. Let me retry with offset 0.\n\nActually, the first get_contacts (no offset) returned 2 contacts. That's suspicious - maybe the default view limit is small. Let me try to find the view limit by searching.\n\nLet me try a more targeted approach. I'll search for each Stockholm contact. Since I need Stockholm contacts 35 or younger, let me search broadly. Let me search for common Swedish first name letters. Actually, let me just try get_contacts with offset values repeatedly - the type error might be a serialization quirk. Let me retry.</think:6124c78e>The search has a view limit and truncates results. I need to enumerate all contacts reliably. Let me retry the offset pagination - the type error may be intermittent.\nThe offset parameter consistently fails. Let me work around it by searching with specific phone prefixes to capture different slices of contacts. Let me search several Swedish mobile prefixes.\nI found the sports coach: **Åsa Lindqvist** (contact_id: b87d40b5953d4872af385577aa14dead), age 31, Sports Coach, Stockholm. She's my girlfriend.\n\nNow I need to find ALL Stockholm contacts 35 or younger except Åsa. Let me continue searching with more prefixes to capture everyone. Let me search additional prefixes.\nThose prefixes returned nothing. The contacts seem to use +4670, +4673 prefixes. But the search view limit truncates results, so I may be missing contacts. Let me search with more specific queries to capture all Stockholm contacts. Let me search by first na", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-82242a99-c57d-4a86-877d-e6403032432d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-ff25bf8c-4199-44d9-b834-418eb56fc9df"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "create_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_ids", "value": "[\"+46700234567\",\"+46701234537\",\"+46202123456\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "title", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-9131cf4a-666f-457f-b355-22cf6bac47d5", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-82242a99-c57d-4a86-877d-e6403032432d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message_to_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "conversation_id", "value": "{{OracleEvent-AGENT-82242a99-c57d-4a86-877d-e6403032432d}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "I'm in a committed relationship now so you shouldn't message anymore", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-d1c1a837-3e97-4759-b29d-ea134347b7bf", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-9131cf4a-666f-457f-b355-22cf6bac47d5"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "The message has been sent.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-7743d877-7f9e-47d0-a8bc-2af58888e385", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-6d490d4b-486f-4523-9eaa-3cd0542e4c87"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Contacts", "function": "delete_contact", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "contact_id", "value": "eabcdec881124416952bcfebbc179285", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-dd6c4de5-fc04-4e0f-a086-6e0bf969e18d", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-6d490d4b-486f-4523-9eaa-3cd0542e4c87"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46202123456", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "This is seriously goodbye", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1c620f4c-5315-40bd-885d-a8d18225cfb8", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-4bdfee10-5e99-4f0e-91e3-dd7f11e4e44c"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46700234567", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "This is seriously goodbye", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-b010ea2e-903e-4db8-955e-0adbb9770c6d", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-4bdfee10-5e99-4f0e-91e3-dd7f11e4e44c"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Contacts", "function": "delete_contact", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "contact_id", "value": "436b35306ffb4799bc8ad5f42e3f8e06", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.14285714285714285, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "time", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 87.38, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 87.38, "prof_tok_in": 471331, "prof_tok_out": 4535, "prof_llm_calls": 26}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:46:05.094420", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_44vlco", "task_desc": "I have a photoshoot this Friday from 7pm-8pm with a bakery brand called Sheryl's Sweets, can you schedule the event and add the person I had a brand partnership meeting with yesterday. I think I recall that the location of the photoshoot will be at the Östermalm Oasis property so book a premium ride there from my house 20 minutes before the photoshoot, but also check with my social media strategist Luísa Silva e Sousa in an email to make sure I heard her right about the location and time of the ", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Find the person I had a brand partnership meeting with yesterday (calendar)\n2. Schedule the photoshoot event Friday 7pm-8pm with that person as attendee\n3. Book a premium ride from my house to Östermalm Oasis 20 min before (6:40pm)\n4. Email social media strategist Luísa Silva e Sousa to confirm location/time\n5. Notify user when email is sent; if wrong, update cab + calendar\n\nLet me start by gathering information.\nI found the key information:\n- **Brand Partnership Meeting yesterday (Mon Oct 14)**: attendee was **Åke Svensson**\n- **Luísa Silva e Sousa** (Social Media Strategist) email: luisa.silvaesousa@gaia2mail.com\n- **My house** (Astrid Lundqvist): Östermalmsgatan 12, 114 39 Stockholm\n\nNow let me schedule the photoshoot event, book the premium ride, and send the confirmation email. The photoshoot is Friday Oct 18, 7pm-8pm. Ride should be 20 min before = 6:40pm.\n\nLet me first check the ride quotation to confirm details, and create the calendar event.\nThe calendar event is created and the ride quotation works. Now let me book the premium ride and send the confirmation email to Luísa.\nThe ride is booked. The email failed because recipients must be a list. Let me fix that.\nThe email has been sent. Now let me notify the user that the email has been sent, as requested.\nI've notified the user. There's a reply from Luísa. Let me read it to check if the details are correct.\nLuísa corrected the details:\n- **Location**: 42 Valhallavägen 30, Stockholm (NOT Östermalm Oasis)\n- **Time**: 7am–8am (NOT 7pm–8pm)\n\nI need to update both the calendar event and the cab booking. The new ride should be 20 min before 7am = 6:40am. Let me update the calendar event, cancel the old ride, and book a new one.\nNow let me update the calendar event with the correct time and location, and book the new ride.\nBoth updates are done. Let me delete the old (incorrect) calendar event to avoid a duplicate.\nAll updates are complete. Let me notify the user of the corrections.\nThe task is now fully complete. Here's a summary of everything that was accomplished:\n\n**1. Found the brand partnership meeting person** — Yesterday's (Mon Oct 14) \"Brand Partnership Meeting\" had attendee **Åke Svensson**.\n\n**2. Scheduled the photoshoot event** — Initially created for Friday Oct 18, 7–8 PM at Östermalm Oasis with Åke Svensson as attendee.\n\n**3. Booked the premium ride** — Initially booked from your house to Östermalm Oasis at 6:40 PM (20 min before).\n\n**4. Emailed Luísa Silva e Sousa** — Sent a confirmation email about the time/location, and notified you when it was sent.\n\n**5. Handled Luísa's correction** — She clarified the correct details were **Friday Oct 18, 7–8 AM** at **42 Valhallavägen 30, Stockholm** (not 7–8 PM at Östermalm Oasis). I then:\n- Updated the calendar event to the correct time/location (deleted the old one)\n- Cancelled the old cab and booked a new Premium ride departing 6:40 AM\n\nAll sub-requests have been completed.\nNo new follow-up message arrived within the wait window. The task is fully complete:\n\n- ✅ Found the brand partnership meeting person (Åke Svensson)\n- ✅ Scheduled the photoshoot calendar event (corrected to Fri Oct 18, 7–8 AM at 42 Valhallavägen 30, Stockholm)\n- ✅ Booked the Premium ride (corrected to depart 6:40 AM)\n- ✅ Emailed Luísa Silva e Sousa to confirm details and notified you when sent\n- ✅ Updated both the calendar event and cab booking after Luísa's correction\n\nNothing further is pending. Let me know if you need any additional changes!", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2f9f65f0-fe85-47b0-bfc1-4674ffc2df94", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f9b73cb4-7b7c-41fa-b780-72c6c9e36c01"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Photoshoot with Sheryl's Sweets", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 19:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 20:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Åke Svensson\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-48a4a4ef-e16a-4703-8e67-fb660b8fe68a", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f9b73cb4-7b7c-41fa-b780-72c6c9e36c01"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "order_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "start_location", "value": "Home", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_location", "value": "Valhallavägen 22, Stockholm", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "service_type", "value": "Premium", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "ride_time", "value": "2024-10-18 18:40:00", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-ce60da21-0d91-409e-a4ec-261714db199c", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f9b73cb4-7b7c-41fa-b780-72c6c9e36c01"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"luisa.silvaesousa@gaia2mail.com\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Confirming Photoshoot Details for Sheryl's Sweets", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Luísa,\n\nI wanted to confirm the location and time of the photoshoot with Sheryl's Sweets this Friday. Is it at Östermalm Oasis (Valhallavägen 22, Stockholm) from 7pm-8pm?\n\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-272d1031-6c67-4b4f-a487-3a0361098ea3", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-ce60da21-0d91-409e-a4ec-261714db199c"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Email sent to Luísa Silva e Sousa.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975823.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-19e05d7a-f0b1-4493-9cac-968b12fd5daa", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-93be4f22-6662-408c-a165-0c9873f6b80b"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "user_cancel_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": []}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975823.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2e46453e-8344-42b7-b737-8530af1e0b80", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-93be4f22-6662-408c-a165-0c9873f6b80b"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "{{OracleEvent-AGENT-2f9f65f0-fe85-47b0-bfc1-4674ffc2df94}}", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975823.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-7dc43a61-f1aa-4cb6-947b-038a32a4cbf9", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-93be4f22-6662-408c-a165-0c9873f6b80b"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Photoshoot with Sheryl's Sweets", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 07:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 08:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Åke Svensson\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975824.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-6a6fadf4-4f3a-4897-bcf0-8ee2f64bf2d8", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-19e05d7a-f0b1-4493-9cac-968b12fd5daa"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "order_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "start_location", "value": "Home", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_location", "value": "42 Valhallavägen 30, Stockholm", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "service_type", "value": "Premium", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "ride_time", "value": "2024-10-18 06:40:00", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.25, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "adaptability", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 