{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:49:11.994714", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_22_3m9r7l", "task_desc": "Delete the calendar event on October 20, 2024 and reschedule all of my calendar events on October 18, 2024 to October 20, 2024 with the same details as before. Send a group email to all of my contacts in Portland, United States to invite them to an all day wine tasting event on October 18, 2024 at my home. Schedule this into my calendar from 08:00:00 to 20:00:00, tagged as personal and the location set to home.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Delete the calendar event on October 20, 2024\n2. Reschedule all calendar events on October 18, 2024 to October 20, 2024 (same details)\n3. Find contacts in Portland, United States\n4. Send group email inviting them to all-day wine tasting on Oct 18, 2024 at home\n5. Add calendar event Oct 18, 2024 08:00-20:00, tagged personal, location home\n\nLet me start by inspecting the calendar events and contacts.\nThe calendar query got cut off. Let me get the full list and fix the contacts call.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me retry the calendar query with integer offset, and continue listing contacts.\nThe tool seems to reject string offsets. Let me try without the offset parameter (defaults to 0).\nThe calendar result is truncated. I need to see all events on Oct 18, 19, and 20. Let me search for events on each date and get the full list of contacts. Let me use search_events and get more contacts.\nSearch by date string doesn't work. Let me get the full calendar events list by querying a wider range, and get all contacts. The earlier query returned events but was truncated. Let me query each day separately with a narrow range to get complete results.\nNow I have a clear picture:\n\n**October 18, 2024 events (to reschedule to Oct 20):**\n1. `4f5f15f11f604f8ea2bab2f1b0d8355b` - Staff Meeting (09:00-10:00)\n2. `e3028e48c650446ba122e787f906df17` - Wine and Food Pairing Research (11:00-13:00)\n3. `9022f9537fec4314880609e923620be6` - Wine Tasting (15:00-18:00)\n4. `49835add11344f388c81f6e65b6a75ed` - Wine Tasting (19:00-21:00)\n\n**October 20, 2024 events:**\n- `20069a91f74c480eba3adeed1ff252c1` - Wine List Review (14:00-16:00) — this is the event to DELETE\n\nNow I need the contacts in Portland, United States. The search returned empty, so let me list all contacts to find them. Let me get the full contacts list.\nThe offset parameter requires an integer but passing \"0\" as string fails. Let me try calling without offset.\nThe result is truncated. I need to see all contacts. The offset parameter fails with string. Let me try passing offset as a number without quotes by using the parameter differently. Since the tool rejects string \"0\", maybe I need to find another way. Let me try with a different value to see if it accepts integers - but I can only pass strings. \n\nLet me try the search_contacts with different queries to find Portland contacts, and also try listing with a higher offset value.\nSearch works on name/phone/email but not city/country. I need to enumerate all contacts to find those in Portland, United States. The get_contacts with offset fails on string. Let me try passing offset as a bare number (the schema may accept it). Let me attempt with offset value that might be parsed as int.\nThe tool strictly requires an int type. Since I can only pass strings, this is a limitation. However, the default call (no offset) returns the first page. Let me check if there's a way to get more. Let me try the InternalContacts tool which may behave differently, and also try get_contacts with a larger limit via the parameter. Actually, the function only has offset. \n\nLet me try InternalContacts__get_contacts to see if it returns more contacts.\nBoth contact tools return the same truncated list. The list is being truncated in display. I need to find all Portland, United States contacts. The search only works on name/phone/email. \n\nLet me try searching for common Portland-area names. But that's unreliable. Let me try the offset with an integer by checking if the tool accepts it when I don't quote it. Actually, the issue is the framework passes it as string. \n\nLet me try a different approach - search for partial email domains or known Portland contacts. Actually, let me reconsider: the truncation might be a display limit. Let me try get_contacts with offset as a number value (no quotes) - the JSON schema might allow it. Let me try once more being careful.\n\nActually, the error is consistent. Let me try searching with various first-name fragments to enumerate. But that's inefficient. \n\nLet me instead try the offset parameter with a numeric literal that the framework might pass as int.\nThe offset parameter consistently fails. The default call returns a truncated list. Let me try searching for contacts by name fragments to enumerate all Portland contacts. I'll search for common first letters. Actually, a better approach: search by email domain \"gaia2mail.com\" won't work since search is on name/phone/email partial match — email might work! Let me try searching by email domain.\nThe search returns the same truncated list (it seems to return all contacts but display is truncated). I need to see the full contact list to identify all Portland, United States contacts. The display truncates after ~4 contacts. \n\nLet me try to get the remaining contacts by searching for specific names. The attendees in the calendar events might be contacts too. Let me search for the names that appear as attendees to find more Portland contacts. But first, let me try to enumerate by searching common name fragments. \n\nActually, a cleaner approach: the search returns ALL matching contacts but the tool output is truncated in display. Let me search for distinctive substrings to page through. Let me search for names starting with different letters to find all contacts. Let me try several searches in parallel.\nThe search returns all contacts but the display truncates. I found a 5th contact: Rodica Dumitrescu (Bucharest, Romania). I need to enumerate ALL contacts to find every Portland, United States one. The display truncates at ~4-5 entries. Let me search with more specific queries to surface later contacts. Let me search for names that would appear later in the list (different letters).\nI'm finding more contacts: Rodica Dumitrescu (Bucharest), Özlem Kalkavan (Istanbul), Adelaide Silva (Porto). The display truncates at ~4 entries, so I'm missing contacts that appear later. I need a systematic way to enumerate all. \n\nThe search returns results but truncates display. Let me search for distinctive letters to surface the rest. Let me try more letters to find contacts I haven't seen yet.\nFound more Portland contacts: **Harold Nakamura** (Portland, United States). And others: Bernadette Fothergill (Houston), Xóchitl García-Ramírez (Edinburgh), Aurelia Șerban (London).\n\nThe display truncates at ~4 entries, so I'm still missing contacts. I need to find ALL Portland, US contacts. Let me continue searching with more letters to surface remaining contacts.\nFound more Portland contacts: **Nadira Jensen** (Portland, United States). And others: Xóchitl García Hernández (Guadalajara), Mehmet Özdemir (Istanbul), Joaquim Pereira (Middlesbrough), Joana Silva (Portuguese).\n\nI'm building the Portland list: Aurélien LaFleur, Kaitlyn McAllister, Harold Nakamura, Nadira Jensen. Let me continue searching remaining letters to find any more contacts.\nFound more contacts: Zeynep Çelik (Leicester), Luísa Silva e Sousa (Porto), Vasco Sousa (Porto). No new Portland ones in these searches. Let me search the remaining letters to be thorough.\nFound more Portland contacts: **Augusta Wynter** (Portland, United States), **Nalani Jensen** (Portland, United States), and **Kaidën Wynter** (Portland - truncated but address shows Portland). Let me get the full Kaidën Wynter details and continue searching remaining letters to ensure completeness.\nKaidën Wynter is in Miami (not Portland). The \"Portland\" search returned empty (search may not match the city field directly). Let me do a few final searches to ensure I've found all Portland contacts, including searching for \"Oregon\" and remaining letters.\nThe search only matches name/phone/email, not city. I've now enumerated contacts across all letters. Let me do a final few searches to catch any remaining contacts I might have missed (letters a, e, i, o, and a couple more).\nI've now thoroughly enumerated the contacts. The search results consistently show the same set of contac", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-fbfabec8-1a5e-4495-bb59-da614de34a86", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-398c1995-6080-4abd-ac7f-fece77d79c8b"], "event_relative_time": 1, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "4f5f15f11f604f8ea2bab2f1b0d8355b", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-f6db1917-a16e-485c-89ef-e194291f94f1", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-398c1995-6080-4abd-ac7f-fece77d79c8b"], "event_relative_time": 1, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "e3028e48c650446ba122e787f906df17", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-d2817917-c5c3-41cb-87b5-a3c70898ca0a", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-398c1995-6080-4abd-ac7f-fece77d79c8b"], "event_relative_time": 1, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": n