{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:49:12.411555", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_xvc7uo", "task_desc": "I need to move out, but my budget is tight at the moment. Delete all properties in Stockholm from my saved apartments list that are not in the 1000-1800 price range. Save all unsaved properties in Stockholm within that price range to my list. If any properties matching my criteria are listed within 4 minutes from now, immediately send a Messages to my friend Linnea Svensson each time a new property within their budget is listed, as she is also looking to move out. Don't notify me, I'll check my ", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll start by understanding the task. Let me break it down:\n1. Delete all saved Stockholm properties NOT in the 1000-1800 price range\n2. Save all unsaved Stockholm properties within 1000-1800 price range\n3. Monitor for new Stockholm properties within budget listed within 4 minutes, and notify Linnea Svensson via Messages each time\n\nLet me first inspect the saved apartments and all apartments to understand the data.\nThe saved list and all apartments results are truncated. Let me get the full lists to identify all Stockholm properties. Let me search specifically for Stockholm properties.\nThe search results are truncated. Let me get the full list of all apartments to see everything, and fix the saved_only parameter type.\nThe list results are truncated at the same point. Let me use the search with price filters to get complete Stockholm results. I'll search Stockholm with min/max price to capture all Stockholm properties in the 1000-1800 range, and also search for Stockholm properties outside that range.\nThe parameters need to be numbers, not strings. Let me retry with proper types.\nThe tool is receiving strings. Let me try passing the numeric values without quotes in the parameter.\nThe search tool seems to coerce to string. Let me instead get the full apartment list by paginating. The list_all_apartments may support offset/limit. Let me try with offset to get the rest of the catalog.\nThe list is truncated at the same point (after \"Lund Living\"). The output is being cut off. Let me try the search_apartments with location only but it's also truncated. The issue is the display truncation. Let me try searching Stockholm with a name filter to narrow results, or use the saved_only properly. Let me retry saved_only as a boolean.\nThe boolean is being passed as a string. Let me try the search with just a name-based query to narrow down Stockholm results so they fit in the output. I'll search by the Stockholm street names I've seen. Actually, let me try searching with a name that's common. Let me search \"Stockholm\" as name.\nThis search by name \"Stockholm\" returns only properties with \"Stockholm\" in the name, not all Stockholm-located ones. I need a complete picture. The output is being truncated. Let me get apartment details for the specific Stockholm properties I've identified so far, and also try to enumerate the full catalog by getting details on each apartment_id.\n\nLet me first record what I know. From searches, Stockholm properties found so far:\n- aae6d8011d49417390f7cdc050c4e39a: Östermalm Oasis, Stockholm, 1800, saved=false\n- 39d8ca5ce03a4fc3adf6ae7ffdf4202b: Stockholm Strand, Stockholm, 2000, saved=false\n- bf9d37569e064982924362e5e6023990: Nordic Oasis, Stockholm, 1800, saved=false\n- 5a8070b881fb4a07bbeffc8b1e9b0109: Stockholm Haven, Stockholm, 1800, saved=true\n- 251d14f5e4fb47f0a148c23b8f5ded2d: Stockholm City Living, Stockholm, 2000, saved=false\n- 094330458b09419599085cbaa62d4999: Stockholm Waterfront, Stockholm, 25000, saved=false\n- a35dab30b0934bb39390ba22b0830be0: Stockholm Söder, Stockholm, 22000, saved=?\n\nI need to find ALL Stockholm properties. The list_all_apartments output truncates. Let me try to get the full list by checking each apartment. Actually, the truncation seems to be a display limit. Let me try searching with a more specific approach - search by location \"Stockholm\" but the result also truncated.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The search by location \"Stockholm\" returned (truncated): Östermalm Oasis, Stockholm Strand, Nordic Oasis, Stockholm Haven, Stockholm City Living... and cut off. \n\nI need the complete list. Let me try getting details on the apartment IDs I have and also probe for more. Let me search with different location spellings or use the saved list which I can get fully.\n\nActually, the best approach: the saved apartments list is what I need to fully enumerate for deletion. Let me get the full saved list. The first list_saved_apartments was truncated too. Let me re-call it and see if I can get more.\n\nLet me try a different tactic - search by location with a zip code prefix for Stockholm (11x xx).\nZip code search returns empty (probably exact match needed or different format). Let me get the full saved apartments list properly. The list_saved_apartments output was truncated. Let me re-call it and carefully read all entries.\nThe output is consistently truncated at the same character count. I need to work around this. The saved list contains Stockholm properties I've identified: 5a8070b881fb4a07bbeffc8b1e9b0109 (Stockholm Haven, 1800, saved=true). \n\nThe truncation is cutting off after \"Uppsala Oasis\". I need to see the rest of the saved list. Let me try to get apartment details for the IDs I have to confirm, and find the complete set of Stockholm saved properties.\n\nThe key challenge: I need the COMPLETE list of saved Stockholm properties to delete those outside 1000-1800, and the complete list of ALL Stockholm properties to save those in range but unsaved.\n\nLet me try searching by location \"Stockholm\" again but I'll need to handle truncation. The search returned (truncated): Östermalm Oasis, Stockholm Strand, Nordic Oasis, Stockholm Haven, Stockholm City Living... cut off.\n\nLet me probe for more Stockholm properties by searching with name fragments. Let me search \"Söder\", \"Norrmalm\", \"Kungsgatan\", \"Valhallavägen\" etc. Actually, a better approach: search by name with common Stockholm district terms.\n\nLet me search several name fragments in parallel.\nGood progress. I'm finding more Stockholm properties. Let me compile what I have and continue searching for more Stockholm properties with other name fragments. I've found these Stockholm properties so far:\n\nStockholm properties found:\n- aae6d8011d49417390f7cdc050c4e39a: Östermalm Oasis, 1800, saved=false\n- 39d8ca5ce03a4fc3adf6ae7ffdf4202b: Stockholm Strand, 2000, saved=false\n- bf9d37569e064982924362e5e6023990: Nordic Oasis, 1800, saved=false\n- 5a8070b881fb4a07bbeffc8b1e9b0109: Stockholm Haven, 1800, saved=true\n- 251d14f5e4fb47f0a148c23b8f5ded2d: Stockholm City Living, 2000, saved=false\n- 094330458b09419599085cbaa62d4999: Stockholm Waterfront, 25000, saved=false\n- a35dab30b0934bb39390ba22b0830be0: Stockholm Söder, 22000, saved=false\n- 862457f415f0486a945965078f0a5a49: Södermalm Delight, 18000, saved=false\n- 63d3239ad97148afa5586d029cd1471b: Södermalm Oasis, 1800, saved=false\n- 26060fbbac9e4f49abdbf9494794e2ad: Södermalm Haven, 1800, saved=false\n\nLet me search more name fragments to find any remaining Stockholm properties.\nI'm building a comprehensive picture. Let me search a few more name fragments to ensure I've found ALL Stockholm properties, particularly looking for any I might have missed. Let me search \"City\", \"View\", \"Luxury\", \"Student\", \"Jewel\", \"Delight\", \"Waterfront\".\nI now have a comprehensive view of the catalog. Let me compile the complete list of Stockholm properties I've found across all searches:\n\n**Stockholm properties (all locations containing \"Stockholm\"):**\n1. aae6d8011d49417390f7cdc050c4e39a: Östermalm Oasis, 1800, saved=false\n2. 39d8ca5ce03a4fc3adf6ae7ffdf4202b: Stockholm Strand, 2000, saved=false\n3. bf9d37569e064982924362e5e6023990: Nordic Oasis, 1800, saved=false\n4. 5a8070b881fb4a07bbeffc8b1e9b0109: Stockholm Haven, 1800, saved=true\n5. 251d14f5e4fb47f0a148c23b8f5ded2d: Stockholm City Living, 2000, saved=false\n6. 094330458b09419599085cbaa62d4999: Stockholm Waterfront, 25000, saved=false\n7. a35dab30b0934bb39390ba22b0830be0: Stockholm Söder, 22000, saved=false\n8. 862457f415f0486a945965078f0a5a49: Södermalm Delight, 18000, saved=false\n9. 63d3239ad97148afa5586d029cd1471b: Södermalm Oasis, 1800, saved=false\n10. 26060fbbac9e4f49abdbf9494794e2ad: Södermalm Haven, 1800, saved=false\n\n**Analysis (price range 1000-1800, inclusive):**\n- In range (1000-1800): #1 (1800), #3 (1800), #4 (1800, saved), #9 (1800), #10 (1800) → all 1800\n- Out of range: #2 (2000), #5 (2000), #6 (25000), #7 (22000), #8 (18000)\n\n**Actions needed:**\n- DELETE from saved: #4 (Stockholm Haven, ", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-d0357843-12aa-4741-8ab4-24c86ed3dd1a", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-5825bc64-3dcd-429d-b0f2-a682c7236163"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "remove_saved_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "6a572b8b24f445cd851709f559a0f8d6", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-4496f394-d3d7-49ee-968e-d1527fb2be45", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-5825bc64-3dcd-429d-b0f2-a682c7236163"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "aae6d8011d49417390f7cdc050c4e39a", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-02c8cafd-0260-47e5-8489-9796890d4cea", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-5825bc64-3dcd-429d-b