nal[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5285cfb9-4c39-4fed-a768-9d768af7bc0b", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-9c13c7d3-d520-4387-a0c4-17511c1d84a2"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "There are multiple Åsa's that have emailed you. Which should I reply to?", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.2857142857142857, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "ambiguity", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 309.65, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 309.65, "prof_tok_in": 245517, "prof_tok_out": 2669, "prof_llm_calls": 13}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:50:07.157176", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_d9my2y", "task_desc": "My friend Linnea Svensson is coming to have dinner and hang out at my place this Friday, create a calendar event for that from 7 PM to 11 PM titled \"Girls Night\". Send her a Messages message asking her to bring energy drinks. Buy a deluxe edition Dungeons and Dragons board game in English so we have something to play. After buying it, book a cab from her address to my address at 6:30 PM, choosing the service type I used the most times for my cab rides last month. Let me know if you're unsure abo", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Create a calendar event \"Girls Night\" Friday 7 PM - 11 PM\n2. Send Linnea a Messages message asking her to bring energy drinks\n3. Buy a deluxe edition D&D board game in English\n4. Book a cab from her address to my address at 6:30 PM using my most-used service type from last month\n5. Report if unsure about anything\n\nLet me start by gathering information: find Linnea's contact (for address & phone), my current user details (my address), and my cab ride history from last month.\nI have Linnea's address (Södermannagatan 12, 118 27 Stockholm, Sweden) and my address (Östermalmsgatan 12, 114 39 Stockholm, Sweden). Now I need to determine my most-used cab service type from last month. Let me get the ride history.\nLet me fix the argument types.\nThe tool seems to require integer types but is receiving strings. Let me try without quotes by passing them differently.\nThe history is truncated. I need to see all 30 rides to determine which service type I used most last month. The current date is 2024-10-15, so \"last month\" is September 2024 (2024-09-01 to 2024-09-30). Let me get the full history.\nThe default call returned 30 rides but truncated the display. Let me try retrieving in smaller chunks to see all entries. I'll try the offset/limit with integer values via a different approach.\nThe parameter validation rejects string inputs. The default call (no args) returned the full 30 rides but the display was truncated. Let me re-call with no args to get the complete data, and I'll need to see all entries. Let me try once more and read carefully.\nThe display truncates at ride 5. I need the full data to count service types per month. Let me try retrieving individual rides by index to see the timestamps and service types for all 30.\nThe integer-typed parameter tools are rejecting my inputs (likely a serialization issue with how arguments are passed). The only working call is `get_ride_history()` with no args, which returns all 30 rides but truncates the display.\n\nLet me reason about what I can see. The timestamps are Unix epoch seconds. Current date is 2024-10-15. Let me convert the visible timestamps:\n- Ride 0: 1725510327 → 2024-09-05 (September)\n- Ride 1: 1728371036 → 2024-10-08 (October)\n- Ride 2: 1723913952 → 2024-08-17 (August)\n- Ride 3: 1724149205 → 2024-08-20 (August)\n- Ride 4: 1726649374 → 2024-09-18 (September)\n- Ride 5: 1726723399 → 2024-09-19 (September)\n\nSo \"last month\" = September 2024. I can see rides 0, 4, 5 are in September. But I need to see all 30 rides to count September service types. The display truncates. Let me try the history call again — perhaps it returns more if I keep reading, or maybe I can get the data in a way that shows later entries. Let me try calling get_ride_history repeatedly; the truncation may be a display limit but I should attempt to see if there's a way.\n\nActually, the issue is the tool output is being truncated in display. Let me try to get the remaining rides by checking if there's pagination. Since offset/limit fail with type errors, I'm limited. \n\nLet me reconsider: maybe I can use get_ride with the index but the type error is because the harness passes strings. Let me try once more with a clean integer call for get_ride_history to see if a different limit helps reveal more. Actually the no-arg version already returns all 30 in the dict but display cuts off.\n\nLet me try calling get_ride_history with no args again — sometimes the truncation is at a fixed character count and I've already seen rides 0-5. I need 6-29. \n\nHmm, the truncation is consistent. Let me think of another approach. Perhaps I can determine September rides differently. The timestamps I have: I need to see all. \n\nLet me try the get_ride tool once more — maybe the type error is intermittent. Actually it's consistent. \n\nGiven the constraint, let me try get_ride_history with no args but I'll need to find a way to see the rest. One option: the tool might accept the args if I don't quote them. But the harness always quotes. \n\nLet me just retry get_ride_history() a couple times to see if the truncation point varies, and meanwhile proceed with the parts of the task I can do now (calendar event, message, shopping). I'll come back to the cab service type determination.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the truncation. The output cut off mid-ride-5. This is a display truncation of the tool result. I cannot change that. \n\nLet me try a different strategy: call get_ride_history with no args and see if I can get later rides by some other means. Since I can't paginate, let me see if maybe the data is sorted by timestamp and I can infer. But I really need the September data.\n\nLet me try get_ride with integer index one more time, perhaps the harness will pass it correctly this time. If it keeps failing, I'll work with what I have and note uncertainty.\n\nActually, let me first do the independent tasks (calendar, message, shopping) and then focus on the cab. Let me proceed with those now in parallel.\n\nFirst, let me find the D&D deluxe board game in English and create the calendar event. I need to determine \"this Friday\" — current date is Tuesday 2024-10-15, so Friday is 2024-10-18.\n\nLet me create the calendar event and search for the game.\nI found the D&D game. The Deluxe English edition has item_id `884ed1a3bb9648e88f7eed8aa60df3d4` (price 67.99). Let me add it to cart and send the message to Linnea. I'll also continue trying to get the full cab history.\nThe message is sent. The cart quantity needs an integer type. The history display keeps truncating at ride 5. I need to see all 30 rides to count September service types. \n\nLet me retry the cart add with integer quantity, and try to get the remaining rides. Since `get_ride_history()` truncates display, let me try `get_ride` with integer index — maybe it works now.\nBoth integer-parameter tools consistently reject my inputs due to a type serialization issue. The `get_ride_history()` (no args) returns all 30 rides but the display truncates after ride 5.\n\nI need the September 2024 rides to determine the most-used service type. Let me think about what I can extract. The display truncates at a fixed character count. I've seen rides 0-5. I need 6-29.\n\nLet me try calling `get_ride_history()` again — perhaps the truncation is based on the result and I should try to get a different view. Actually, since I can't paginate, let me try a creative approach: maybe `list_rides` between two locations could help, but that won't give history.\n\nAlternatively, I can reason: the task says \"the service type I used the most times for my cab rides last month.\" Last month = September 2024. I've confirmed rides 0, 4, 5 are in September. I need to see the rest.\n\nLet me try get_ride_history once more and carefully note — maybe if I call it, the truncation might show a different portion. Actually it's deterministic. \n\nLet me try the integer tools with a different format. The error says \"got <class 'str'>\". Perhaps the harness needs me to pass the integer without it being wrapped. There's no way for me to control that.\n\nGiven the constraints, let me try get_ride_history() a few more times to see if I can capture later rides through some variation. Actually, let me reconsider — maybe the truncation is in the rendering and the actual data is there but cut. I cannot access it.\n\nLet me try one more thing: call get_ride_history with no args but maybe the system will eventually show more. I'll just retry and see if ride 6+ appears. If not, I'll need to make a decision based on available data and flag uncertainty.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole approach. The most reliable path: I have 6 of 30 rides visible. Among September rides visible (0, 4, 5): Van, Premium, Default. That's not enough.\n\nLet me try get_ride_history() again to confirm truncation is fixed, and also try the integer-typed get_ride one more time in case it's flaky.\nThe display consistently truncates at ride 5, and the integer-typed tools (`get_ride`, `get_r", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-c53f0052-c525-4479-aced-f955619c8e83", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-72578366-50ea-4767-a08d-4c5b87aed88c"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46700234567", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Linnea, can you bring energy drinks on Friday?", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-91433544-1c41-4fce-83d4-a8c0a8d8ff60", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-72578366-50ea-4767-a08d-4c5b87aed88c"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "884ed1a3bb9648e88f7eed8aa60df3d4", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "1", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5649d714-65d2-43c3-97a7-00883053d84e", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-91433544-1c41-4fce-83d4-a8c0a8d8ff60"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "checkout", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "discount_code", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-6bc71c0f-26b8-44f9-8045-235b292a8ca2", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-72578366-50ea-4767-a08d-4c5b87aed88c"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Girls Night", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 19:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 23:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "Home", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-56709e3e-4273-43d9-859b-1a37e8bef8e1", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-5649d714-65d2-43c3-97a7-00883053d84e"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Please clarify the preferred service type, as you used 'Default' and 'Van' service type equally often last month", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.4, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "ambiguity", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 319.35, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 319.35, "prof_tok_in": 465932, "prof_tok_out": 8066, "prof_llm_calls": 23}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:50:07.157397", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_4o5b3h", "task_desc": "Send a Messages message to Axel in my one-on-one conversation with him asking if he still wants to meet for coffee as I haven't received a calendar invite from him yet, and invite him to join me on this Friday at 2:00pm at the Coffee Shop located at Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm. Set up the event in my calendar for an hour on that day and name it \"Coffee Break with Axel\". Book a default cab to pick me up 30 minutes ahead of our coffee break from Home to the Coffee Shop. Let me know when y", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll start by gathering the information I need: finding Axel's contact info, checking my calendar for Friday, and understanding the current state. Let me make several independent calls.\nI found Axel's ID (+46202123456) and the current time. Friday is 2024-10-18. Let me check the existing conversation with Axel and look at Friday's calendar to confirm availability.\nFriday 2024-10-18 at 2:00pm is free (only a 10-12 session and 18:00 yoga). Now let me find the one-on-one conversation with Axel. The second conversation shows Axel (+46202123456) and +46734567890 — let me check who that is to confirm it's a one-on-one with me.\nThe second conversation (d9e8aed8d70c46e3a22eea360f8328f2) is a group with Åsa and Axel. The other conversation with Axel (+46202123456) and Astrid (+46734567890) is a one-on-one between Astrid and Axel — not me. \n\nI need to find my one-on-one with Axel. Let me check my current user details to know my own ID, and search for conversations.\nI'm Astrid (+46734567890). There's a one-on-one conversation with Axel at conversation_id `bd5fd1ae6f9947dda2e6631c4cde1773`. Let me read it to confirm it's our one-on-one.\nThis is my one-on-one conversation with Axel. He mentioned he'd send a calendar invite for next week but I haven't received one. Now let me do the 3 tasks:\n\n1. Send the message to Axel\n2. Create the calendar event\n3. Book the cab\n\nLet me do all three now.\nAll three tasks are done. Now I need to handle the conditional: \"If Axel is not available, reschedule...\" This depends on Axel's reply. The task also says to wait for any Messages from others with event invites and ignore them. Let me wait for Axel's response (or other messages) before finalizing.\n\nLet me wait for a notification from Axel.\nThere are new messages. The one in my conversation with Axel (bd5fd1ae6f9947dda2e6631c4cde1773) is likely from Axel. The other two conversations (c70dd0c5720e44b4a02e725661239284 and ca0fc7c4f01f4a6ca44a329ac3836633) are from others — possibly event invites which I should ignore. Let me read the Axel conversation to see his reply.\nThe parameters need to be integers. Let me retry.\nThe tool seems to require integer types but is receiving strings. Let me try without the offset parameter, just limit.\nAxel replied: he's NOT available on Friday, but is available the following Monday or Tuesday at 2:00pm. So I need to:\n1. Reschedule the Coffee Break to the earliest day we're both available (Monday 2024-10-21 at 2pm)\n2. Rebook the cab\n3. Reply to Axel confirming the new date\n\nLet me first check my calendar for Monday 2024-10-21 and Tuesday 2024-10-22 to confirm availability, and check the other two conversations to verify they're event invites (to ignore). Let me also check Monday/Tuesday availability.\nConfirmed:\n- The two other messages are event invites from Beshoy (+4531123458, coffee invite) and Nomsa (+33612345678, anniversary gathering) — I will ignore them as instructed.\n- My calendar: Monday 2024-10-21 is free at 2pm (only 10-12 session and 18:00 yoga). Tuesday 2024-10-22 has a Brand Partnership Meeting 14:00-16:00, so 2pm is NOT free on Tuesday. The earliest day we're both available is **Monday 2024-10-21 at 2:00pm**.\n\nNow I'll:\n1. Delete the Friday event and create the Monday event\n2. Cancel the Friday cab and book the Monday cab (pickup 13:30)\n3. Reply to Axel confirming Monday\nAll actions are complete. Let me verify the final state of the calendar event and confirm everything is in order.\nEverything is done. Here's a summary of what I completed:\n\n**Initial 3 tasks (Friday plan):**\n1. ✅ Sent a Messages message to Axel in our one-on-one conversation asking if he still wants to meet for coffee (since I hadn't received his calendar invite) and inviting him to Friday 10/18 at 2:00pm at the Coffee Shop (Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm).\n2. ✅ Created the \"Coffee Break with Axel\" calendar event for Friday 10/18, 2:00–3:00pm.\n3. ✅ Booked a Default cab from Home to the Coffee Shop for 1:30pm (30 min before).\n\n**Follow-up (Axel was not available):**\nAxel replied that he's not free Friday but is available Monday or Tuesday at 2:00pm. I checked my calendar — Tuesday 10/22 has a Brand Partnership Meeting at 2:00pm, so the earliest day we're both free is **Monday, October 21 at 2:00pm**. I then:\n- ✅ Deleted the Friday event and recreated \"Coffee Break with Axel\" for **Monday 10/21, 2:00–3:00pm** at the same Coffee Shop.\n- ✅ Cancelled the Friday cab and rebooked a Default cab from Home to the Coffee Shop for **Monday 10/21 at 1:30pm**.\n- ✅ Replied to Axel confirming Monday the 21st at 2:00pm works and gave him the location.\n\n**Other messages:** I received event-invite Messages from Beshoy (coffee next Wednesday) and Nomsa (anniversary gathering Friday) — per your instructions, I ignored both and left them for you to reply to later.\nAll tasks are complete. Let me deliver the final summary to the user.\nI've delivered the final summary to the user. All parts of the task are complete:\n\n1. ✅ Sent the message to Axel in our one-on-one conversation\n2. ✅ Created the \"Coffee Break with Axel\" calendar event (rescheduled to Monday Oct 21, 2–3pm after Axel said he was unavailable Friday)\n3. ✅ Booked the Default cab (rebooked for Monday Oct 21 at 1:30pm)\n4. ✅ Replied to Axel confirming the new date\n5. ✅ Ignored the event-invite messages from Beshoy and Nomsa as instructed\n\nThe task is fully handled.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a2da3f6f-4d4e-4100-9db7-c9398d589afc", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-20c3836c-4d47-445c-b1a3-94851d8e8a80"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46202123456", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Axel, still up for coffee? Haven't received a calendar invite from you yet. Want to meet this Friday at 2:00pm at the Coffee Shop on Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm?", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-86a0ea2a-d1d1-4ffc-8814-0237c8a757c1", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-20c3836c-4d47-445c-b1a3-94851d8e8a80"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Coffee Break with Axel", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 14:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 15:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-58ad028a-09f0-486d-9687-036a500da96b", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-20c3836c-4d47-445c-b1a3-94851d8e8a80"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "order_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "start_location", "value": "Home", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_location", "value": "Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "service_type", "value": "Default", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "ride_time", "value": "2024-10-18 13:30:00", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975783.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-c6e1e696-5a5d-4cca-98eb-238fdf902994", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-d64a4014-962e-47f6-8ebb-199da7a18771"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "{{OracleEvent-AGENT-86a0ea2a-d1d1-4ffc-8814-0237c8a757c1}}", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975783.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5d91a1e7-4be0-4f68-b7b0-4202477eeb3d", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-d64a4014-962e-47f6-8ebb-199da7a18771"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Coffee Break with Axel", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-21 14:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-21 15:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975783.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-e957c13c-fe23-4728-90e8-c3a7f8b372cd", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-d64a4014-962e-47f6-8ebb-199da7a18771"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "user_cancel_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": []}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975783.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-4d59182e-276a-4961-82e7-ba3cebc08ee9", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-d64a4014-962e-47f6-8ebb-199da7a18771"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46202123456", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Axel, let's do our coffee break on Monday, Oct 21st at 2:00pm at the Coffee Shop, Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm.", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975784.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-947f9837-f9b5-4fcb-b8ad-5488789a9844", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-e957c13c-fe23-4728-90e8-c3a7f8b372cd"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "order_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "start_location", "value": "Home", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_location", "value": "Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "service_type", "value": "Default", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "ride_time", "value": "2024-10-21 13:30:00", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-158e25f8-a1c0-4b92-ace8-9d578bb26515", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-a2da3f6f-4d4e-4100-9db7-c9398d589afc", "OracleEvent-AGENT-86a0ea2a-d1d1-4ffc-8814-0237c8a757c1", "OracleEvent-AGENT-58ad028a-09f0-486d-9687-036a500da96b"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Those 3 actions have been completed.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.2222222222222222, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "adaptability", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 277.87, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 277.87, "prof_tok_in": 328351, "prof_tok_out": 3190, "prof_llm_calls": 17}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:50:24.607217", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_gp0nd0", "task_desc": "Find the document in my news folder about Dr. Jensen CISA allegations. Share this document with my contacts from Stockholm that are 21 to 44 years old, excluding myself, letting them know that this is an important document I wanted to share with them. If the person has Messages - send it through Messages, otherwise send it through Chats. Send each message separately, and let me know how many people did you send the document too.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll start by exploring the news folder to find the document about Dr. Jensen CISA allegations.\nLet me check the root directory structure.\nLet me look at the Documents folder more thoroughly to find the news folder.\nThere are many files. Let me search for the document about Dr. Jensen CISA allegations. I'll search the content of these files.\nLet me search for the specific content using a different approach. I'll grep through the files. Let me try reading a few files to understand the format, then search. Actually, let me use the search functionality by reading files. Let me try cat on a single file first.\nThe files appear to be empty when read directly. Let me try reading with read_document instead.\nThe files seem empty. Let me check the file info to understand. Let me look at a few files with info.\nThe file is 0 bytes. Many files may be empty. Let me check the info of all files to find which ones have content. Let me list with detail.\nAll files appear to be 0 bytes. The list was truncated. Let me get the full list to find files with non-zero size. Let me check the total count and look for files with content.\nThe list is truncated. Let me check the detail view to find files with non-zero size. The detail view showed all 0 bytes so far. Let me get the full detail listing to find any file with content. Let me try reading the files that have unusual names (with underscores like metro_herald_73_587.txt and metro_herald_89_722.txt) which might be the actual content files.\nAll files in the news folder appear empty. The detail listing showed all 0 bytes. Let me get the complete detail listing to be thorough and confirm there are no files with content. Let me check the full list with detail - I need to see all files. Let me try a different approach to find files with content.\nThe detail listing is truncated at the same point. The files all appear to be 0 bytes. Let me check the wiki folder and other locations, as the document might be elsewhere. But first, let me verify by checking the full count of files and whether any have content. Let me look at the Documents folder structure more carefully - maybe there's a subfolder. Let me also check if there are other news-related files. Let me search the entire filesystem for \"Jensen\" or \"CISA\".\nThe tree view shows different files (daily_chronicle_news) than the ls view (metro_herald). The ls view was showing cached/truncated data. The tree shows the actual files. Let me read one of these daily_chronicle files to check content.\nStill empty. The tree view shows the real filenames but they're all empty. Let me get the complete tree to see all files, and check if any have content. Let me look at the full tree output - it was truncated. Let me search for files that might contain \"Jensen\" by reading the full tree.\nThe tree is also truncated. The files appear to be empty (0 bytes). This is strange. Let me check the file info on one of the daily_chronicle files to confirm, and also check if there's a different representation. Let me verify the actual size.\nAll files are 0 bytes. The news folder contains empty placeholder files. This is unusual. Let me reconsider - perhaps the document is stored elsewhere, or perhaps the content needs to be accessed differently. Let me check the wiki folder and the benchmarks folder, and also search the whole filesystem. Let me also check if there's a \"Documents\" with the actual content. Let me look at the full tree of Documents.\nThe news folder files are all empty (0 bytes). This is a problem - the document content isn't readable. However, the task is about finding the document and sharing it. The document is identified by its filename/title in the news folder. Let me reconsider - perhaps the file content is accessible through a different method. Let me try opening the file with the open tool to read it.\nThe open returned empty. The files are genuinely empty. Let me reconsider the task. The document is about \"Dr. Jensen CISA allegations\" in the news folder. The files are named by newspaper and year ranges. I need to find which one is about Dr. Jensen. Since the content is empty, I cannot search by content. \n\nLet me reconsider - maybe the ls view (metro_herald) and tree view (daily_chronicle) are showing different things because of caching. Let me re-examine. The ls showed metro_herald files, the tree showed daily_chronicle files. These are different sets. Let me get a complete and accurate listing. Let me try the ls again and capture the full output.\n\nActually, the issue might be that the file content is genuinely empty in this environment, but the task expects me to identify the document by its name. Let me think about what \"Dr. Jensen CISA allegations\" document would be named. \n\nLet me get the complete list of files in the news folder to find one that might relate to Jensen. Let me try reading the full tree by checking if there's a way to see all files. The tree was truncated. Let me look at the wiki folder too since it might have related content.\n\nActually, let me step back. The files are empty, so I cannot determine content. But maybe the task is designed so that the document exists with content. Let me re-verify by trying to read a file via cat with the full path including leading slash.\nThe files are confirmed empty. Let me reconsider the whole approach. Perhaps the document isn't in the news folder's text files but the task wants me to find it. Let me search the entire filesystem for \"Jensen\" or \"CISA\" using the search tools available. There's no global file search tool, but let me check the wiki folder and other folders. Let me also reconsider - maybe the news folder has a different structure with actual content files.\n\nLet me look at the complete tree of the news folder by reading it in a way that shows all files. The tree output was truncated. Let me check if there are subdirectories in news.\nThe ls consistently shows metro_herald files (all 0 bytes), while tree shows daily_chronicle files. There's a discrepancy - possibly the ls is showing a cached/limited view. Both sets appear empty. \n\nLet me reconsider. The task says \"Find the document in my news folder about Dr. Jensen CISA allegations.\" Given the files are empty, perhaps the document identification is by filename. But none of the filenames mention Jensen. \n\nLet me check the wiki folder which might contain the actual document, and also check if there's a way the content is stored. Let me look at the wiki folder.\nThe tree shows the full filesystem. The news folder files are all empty. This is a known pattern in these simulations where the news files are empty placeholders, but the task expects me to identify the document. \n\nLet me reconsider. The discrepancy between ls (metro_herald) and tree (daily_chronicle) is concerning. Let me get the complete and accurate file listing. The ls tool seems to be returning a different/limited set. Let me try to get the full list by checking the actual count. \n\nActually, the key issue: the files are empty so I can't read content. But the task is about sharing a document. Perhaps the document is identified by its title/filename and I just need to share the file path. Let me focus on finding which file is about Dr. Jensen.\n\nGiven the files are empty, I cannot search content. But maybe the task is designed such that there IS a file with content about Jensen. Let me re-examine - the ls showed metro_herald files, tree showed daily_chronicle files. These are two different listings of the same folder? That can't be right unless there are many files and both are truncated differently.\n\nLet me get the complete picture. Let me count files and look for any with content. Let me try reading several daily_chronicle files to find one with content. But they're all 0 bytes per info.\n\nWait - maybe the issue is that the file content is stored but the read tools return empty due to some encoding. Let me try the read_document on a daily_chronicle file with a higher max_lines and see. Already tried - empty.\n\nLe", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-ceae03f2-d123-4f9b-b030-c10eab084644", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-150029c6-696d-4f89-876a-4d32b8673a28"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46700234567", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey! I wanted to share this important document with you.", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "Documents/news/daily_chronicle_news_2020_2025_125.txt", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-d8a3390c-3546-471f-8db1-519aa40b44c1", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-150029c6-696d-4f89-876a-4d32b8673a28"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46731234567", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey! I wanted to share this important document with you.", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "Documents/news/daily_chronicle_news_2020_2