{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T10:51:47.196070", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_5flf8t", "task_desc": "Find the three most recent emails that have Collaboration within the subject line. Schedule a meeting every day for the next three days, beginning tomorrow, using the email's subject line as the title of the calendar event. The most recent email should be the subject of tomorrow's event, the next most recent email is for the day after tomorrow, and so on. The time for each event is 7am for one hour via Zoom. After each event is scheduled, then reply to the individual emails letting the sender kn", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll start by finding the three most recent emails with \"Collaboration\" in the subject line.\nLet me get more details on these emails and search more thoroughly to find all emails with \"Collaboration\" in the subject.\nThe search seems to return truncated results. Let me search with different terms to find all collaboration emails and get the full list.\nThe search returns truncated content. Let me list emails with proper integer types to see all emails and find the collaboration ones.\nThe tool requires integer types. Let me try without quotes by passing them differently.\nThe list is also truncated. Let me get the full content of the second email and search for more collaboration emails with different terms.\nThe search results are truncated. I need to find the third email. Let me search with different terms and also check the SENT folder.\nI found a third email. Let me get the full details of the third email to confirm its timestamp.\nThere are more than three. I need to find ALL emails with \"Collaboration\" in the subject and determine the three most recent by timestamp. Let me search with broader terms to capture all of them.\nThe search results are being truncated in display. Let me search for the remaining emails with different subject fragments to capture all of them and their timestamps.\nI now have 5 emails with \"Collaboration\" in the subject. Let me compile the timestamps:\n\n1. **bb64c3792e0a40208957cfc9e09d0692** - \"Collaboration Opportunity for Swedish Fashion Brands\" - Yuting Liang - timestamp 1728827076.34 (most recent)\n2. **71c6b7b7b7ee4598a5616a4729997164** - \"Collaboration Opportunity for a Social Media Campaign\" - João Silva - timestamp 1728819952.47\n3. **101c3a6a1fa247139016334ad31460f4** - \"Collaboration Opportunity for Fashion Brand Campaign\" - Axel Lindqvist - timestamp 1728559647.79\n4. **075047b041984472a7d50dbc0baf7796** - \"Collaboration Opportunity for Fashion Brand Campaign\" - Aurélien Dumont - timestamp 1723834710.76\n\nThe three most recent are #1 (Yuting), #2 (João), #3 (Axel). Let me verify the current date and confirm the timestamps ordering.\nCurrent sim time is 2024-10-15. The three most recent emails with \"Collaboration\" in the subject are:\n\n1. **Yuting Liang** (1728827076.34) - \"Collaboration Opportunity for Swedish Fashion Brands\" → Tomorrow (Oct 16)\n2. **João Silva** (1728819952.47) - \"Collaboration Opportunity for a Social Media Campaign\" → Day after tomorrow (Oct 17)\n3. **Axel Lindqvist** (1728559647.79) - \"Collaboration Opportunity for Fashion Brand Campaign\" → Oct 18\n\nLet me schedule the three calendar events (7am-8am via Zoom).\nAll three events are scheduled. Now let me reply to each email with the meeting details.\nAll three replies have been sent. Now let me send a message to the user letting them know the emails have been sent and events scheduled.\nNow I'll wait for any follow-up replies from the senders, as instructed in the task.\nThree new emails arrived. Let me check the inbox to see who replied.\nThe list view is truncated. Let me search for the new replies by looking at recent emails. Let me search for reply-related terms.\nNo results for those terms. The new emails may have different subjects. Let me search for each sender's name to find their replies.\nThe search isn't showing the new replies clearly. The three new emails arrived at the same timestamp. Let me list the inbox with a larger limit to see all emails including the new ones.\nThe tool requires integer types. Let me try without quotes by passing them differently.\nThe list view truncates content. The new emails arrived at timestamp 1728975941.84. Let me search for content that would be in replies, like \"works\" or \"schedule\" or \"time\" to find the new replies.\nThe search isn't finding the new replies. Let me try searching for common reply phrases and the senders' reply addresses.\nThe search isn't returning the new emails. The new emails arrived at timestamp 1728975941.84. Let me try reading emails by index to find the newest ones. Let me check the most recent indices.\nThe tool requires integer types but the schema passes strings. Let me try a different approach and search for the new emails by their likely content. The three new emails arrived simultaneously. Let me search for terms that might be in replies.\nThe search results show existing emails but not the new replies. The three new emails arrived at timestamp 1728975941.84. Let me search for the senders' names who might have replied, and also try searching for \"reply\" or \"response\" content. Let me also check if the new emails are from the same three senders (Yuting, João, Axel) as replies.\nThe search isn't surfacing the new replies. The three new emails arrived at timestamp 1728975941.84. Let me try reading emails by index using integer values. The tool seems to reject string types. Let me try the get_email_by_index with a numeric approach - perhaps the issue is the parameter serialization. Let me try listing with offset/limit as integers.\nThe list_emails tool is rejecting string parameters. Let me try the get_email_by_index with a numeric value to read the newest emails. The new emails are at the top (most recent). Let me try index 0.\nThe integer parameter issue persists. Let me try the search_emails with different query terms that might match the new reply content. The new emails arrived at 1728975941.84. Let me search for terms likely in replies about scheduling.\nThe search tool isn't surfacing the new reply emails. The three new emails arrived at timestamp 1728975941.84. The search seems to only return older emails. Let me try reading emails by index with a numeric value - the issue may be that I need to pass the integer differently. Let me try the get_email_by_id approach by guessing, or try search with the exact new timestamp context.\n\nLet me try searching for content that would be unique to replies - perhaps the replies reference \"October\" or \"tomorrow\" or \"morning\".\nThe search tool consistently returns only older emails and not the three new replies that arrived at timestamp 1728975941.84. The new emails are the most recent in the inbox. Let me try reading them by index. The tool requires integer types - let me try passing the index as a number without quotes by using the get_email_by_index with a different format. \n\nActually, the issue is the parameter serialization. Let me try the get_email_by_id with the parent_id pattern, or try reading the most recent emails. Since the new emails are at the top of the inbox (most recent), let me try index values. The error says it got a string - perhaps I should try a value that the system interprets as int. Let me try with the literal number.\nThe get_email_by_index tool consistently rejects the parameter type. Let me try a different strategy - the new emails are replies to my three sent emails. They likely have parent_id set to my sent email IDs. Let me search the SENT folder and also try searching with the reply senders' names combined with likely reply content. \n\nActually, let me reconsider. The three new emails arrived at 1728975941.84. They are the most recent. The search tool may have a limit on how many it returns or may not index them yet. Let me try searching for the specific reply senders who would respond - the three I emailed: Yuting Liang, João Silva, Axel Lindqvist. I already searched those. \n\nLet me try searching for partial content that a reply might contain, like \"Zoom\" or \"7am\" or \"meeting\" - I tried meeting. Let me try \"Zoom\" and \"schedule\".\nThe search tool is not surfacing the three new reply emails that arrived at timestamp 1728975941.84. These are the most recent emails in the inbox. The get_email_by_index tool has a type bug. Let me try the get_email_by_id with the parent_id of my sent emails - the replies likely have parent_id set to my sent email IDs. Let me first check my sent emails to get their IDs.\nThe list_emails tool also has the integer type bug. Let me try the get_email_by_id tool with the parent_id values from my sent emails. M", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-d715c0a8-3e04-42bd-833b-6d3c041d72d6", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-8b3b2aca-1574-4d57-80b2-6bac54bf3994"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Collaboration Opportunity for Swedish Fashion Brands", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 07:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 08:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "Zoom", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-91c2693b-15a4-41e0-9950-0cbce5145c41", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-8b3b2aca-1574-4d57-80b2-6bac54bf3994"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Collaboration Opportunity for a Social Media Campaign", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-17 07:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-17 08:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "Zoom", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-da798b50-cbb5-44a8-8381-4b7f38a36a0d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-8b3b2aca-1574-4d57-80b2-6bac54bf3994"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Collaboration Opportunity: Raising Awareness about Public Health", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 07:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 08:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "Zoom", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-b31654de-8b49-4d5a-ae5b-83e9e6fb08e8", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-d715c0a8-3e04-42bd-833b-6d3c041d72d6"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "reply_to_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "bb64c3792e0a40208957cfc9e09d0692", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Yuting Liang,\n\nI have scheduled a meeting for October 16, 2024 from 7 AM to 8 AM via Zoom to discuss the collaboration opportunity. Does this date and time work for you? If not, please reply with your preferred date and time.\n\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-dffeced1-ba5f-465d-8819-c8f6e5ae99dd", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-91c2693b-15a4-41e0-9950-0cbce5145c41"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "reply_to_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "71c6b7b7b7ee4598a5616a4729997164", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Joao,\n\nI have scheduled a meeting for October 17, 2024, from 7 AM to 8 AM via Zoom to discuss the collaboration opportunity. Does this date and time work for you? If not, please reply with your preferred date and time.\n\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-ca9b69d6-0550-488b-9091-aca2b75d64ba", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-da798b50-cbb5-44a8-8381-4b7f38a36a0d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "reply_to_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "369b7918d5e042d3a531c226bfd9c212", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Astrid Kjeldsen,\n\nI have scheduled a meeting for October 18, 2024, from 7 AM to 8 A