{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:03:26.882919", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_gjw61a", "task_desc": "Schedule a Property Tour event at the most expensive 4 bedroom property in my saved list for this Saturday from 4pm - 5pm. Add the participants of the the most recently updated Messages conversation 'Catching up with friends' as attendees (besides me). Book me a premium cab from Stora Södergatan 25, Lund to the property location (including the zip code) one hour before the property tour starts. Send each of the attendees separate Messages messages with the time and place of the tour. If a new fu", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Find the most expensive 4-bedroom property in my saved list\n2. Find the most recently updated Messages conversation 'Catching up with friends' and its participants\n3. Schedule a Property Tour event this Saturday 4-5pm with those attendees\n4. Book a premium cab from Stora Södergatan 25, Lund to the property (with zip code) one hour before\n5. Send each attendee a separate Messages message with time and place\n6. Monitor for 3 minutes for a new furnished 4-bedroom property in same zip code that's more expensive; if found, move everything and notify attendees\n\nLet me start by gathering the needed information.\nThe saved apartments list was truncated. Let me get the full list and find the 'Catching up with friends' conversation. The search returned many conversation IDs. Let me get the full saved list and check the conversations.\nThe saved apartments list keeps getting truncated. Let me use the search function with a filter for 4 bedrooms and saved_only to find the 4-bedroom properties. Also let me fix the conversation listing with integer types.\nThe parameters need to be integers, not strings. Let me retry with proper types.\nThe tool is receiving strings. Let me try passing the integer values without quotes in the parameter format.\nThe integer parameters are being passed as strings. Let me try a different approach - I'll list all apartments and filter myself, and for messages I'll read the conversations from the search results. Let me first get the full saved apartments list by reading it properly. Let me try listing all apartments.\nThe list is large and truncated. Let me get the full saved apartments list. The saved list was truncated at \"8fb973f7cd694f589755f5755a0dd8ba\". Let me try to get the complete saved list by reading it. Since the output is truncated, let me try the search with saved_only but I need to handle the integer issue. \n\nLet me try a different approach for the integer parameters - perhaps the issue is the JSON serialization. Let me retry the saved search with the integer parameter.\nThe boolean is also being passed as a string. There seems to be a serialization issue with non-string types. Let me try the search with just the bedrooms filter as a string but the tool expects int. \n\nLet me instead get the complete saved apartments list. The list_saved_apartments output was truncated. Let me try reading it again - maybe I can get more by checking each apartment. Actually, let me try the search_apartments with number_of_bedrooms as a proper integer value. The issue might be how I'm formatting. Let me try once more being careful.\nThe tool consistently receives strings. Let me work with what I have. I'll get the complete saved apartments list by listing all apartments and filtering for saved + 4 bedrooms. The list_all_apartments was also truncated. Let me try to get the full list - perhaps I need to page through. But there's no offset param. \n\nLet me re-examine: the saved list showed 5 apartments before truncation (62cb7292..., d8f02d5..., 256aeabd..., 49c463a..., 8fb973f7...). The 8fb973f7 was cut off mid-entry. Let me get the details of that apartment and also check if there are more saved ones. Let me get the full saved list by trying list_saved_apartments again and capturing more.\n\nActually, the truncation is a display issue. Let me try to get apartment details for the truncated one and search for 4-bedroom saved properties differently. Let me get details on 8fb973f7cd694f589755f5755a0dd8ba.\nThat's a 2-bedroom. The saved list had 5 entries shown but truncated. I need the complete list to find all 4-bedroom saved properties. Let me try listing all apartments with a larger view - the list_all was truncated too. Let me page through by getting more. Since there's no offset, let me try the search with min_price to reduce results, or try to get the full saved list.\n\nLet me try list_saved_apartments once more and see if I can get the complete output. The truncation might be consistent. Let me think - I saw 5 saved apartments. But there could be more after the truncation point. Let me try searching all apartments with a high min price to see the expensive ones, and also try to enumerate saved ones.\n\nActually, a better approach: let me search all apartments filtered by 4 bedrooms to find which 4-bedroom properties exist, then cross-reference with saved. But the integer issue blocks that. \n\nLet me try the search_apartments with string that might be coerced. Actually the error is clear - it needs int. The framework is passing my value as string. Let me try writing the number without it being interpreted as string - perhaps using a different representation.\n\nLet me just try listing all apartments and capture the full output by requesting it. The truncation seems to be at a character limit. Let me try list_all_apartments again - maybe it returns the same. I'll need to find a way to see all saved 4-bedroom properties.\n\nLet me try get_apartment_details on the remaining saved IDs I might be missing. But I don't know all IDs. \n\nAlternative: Let me re-call list_saved_apartments and carefully note all entries. The first call showed entries ending at 8fb973f7 (Uppsala Oasis, 2br). There may be more saved apartments after it that got truncated. Let me try to get them by searching with saved_only - but bool issue.\n\nLet me try a creative approach: search_apartments with a name filter that's empty won't work. Let me just retry list_saved_apartments and see if output differs.\nThe output is consistently truncated at the same point (after Uppsala Oasis). This is a display truncation. I need to find if there are more saved apartments. Let me try the search_apartments with saved_only as a boolean - the issue is serialization. Let me try passing it differently. \n\nActually, let me try the search with a string \"true\" - no, it needs bool. The framework seems to wrap everything as string. Let me try the integer/boolean parameters one more time but maybe the framework will accept if I just provide the raw value. \n\nLet me try a workaround: search all apartments by location or name to find 4-bedroom ones, then check saved status. But I need to see the full catalog. The list_all was also truncated. \n\nLet me try searching with a min_price filter to reduce output size so it doesn't truncate, which might reveal more saved 4-bedroom properties. Let me try search_apartments with just a high min_price.\nAll numeric parameters are being passed as strings. This is a framework serialization limitation. Let me work around it by getting the full saved list through individual detail lookups. \n\nI know the saved list has at least these 5: 62cb7292 (3br), d8f02d5d (1br), 256aeabd (3br), 49c463a0 (2br), 8fb973f7 (2br). The truncation cut off after 8fb973f7. There may be more saved apartments. \n\nLet me try to find all 4-bedroom properties in the full catalog by listing all apartments and capturing the complete output. The list_all was truncated at \"fd4ef3ea31944569b8a9f330bcf51369\" (Lund Living, 1br). Let me get details on that and continue enumerating. But I don't have all IDs.\n\nBetter approach: Let me try the search_apartments with number_of_bedrooms but the framework needs int. Since it keeps failing, let me try a completely different value format. Perhaps the issue is that I need to not quote it. Let me try once more with the integer written plainly.\n\nActually, I've tried multiple times. The framework is converting to string. Let me instead enumerate the full catalog via list_all_apartments and get details on each to find 4-bedroom saved ones. But I can't see all IDs due to truncation.\n\nLet me try list_all_apartments again - it might show different portion or I can capture the IDs I see and get details. The truncation showed these IDs so far:\n- aae6d801 (2br, not saved)\n- 835cacdf (1br, not saved)\n- 92ba401d (2br, saved)\n- 0d836a21 (1br, not saved)\n- fd4ef3ea (1br, Lund Living)\n\nLet me get details on fd4ef3ea and continue. Actually this is inefficie", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-8e4fcf55-b253-4826-a081-834aa43ca375", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-df17e0e3-7061-4137-8c72-3460f5a7f280"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Property Tour", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 16:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 17:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "Lund Luxury Living, Klostergatan 15, Lund 222 22", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Åsa Lundqvist\",\"Astrid Rasmussen\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1feb05f2-6fea-4477-b3aa-d4c35a893514", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-df17e0e3-7061-4137-8c72-3460f5a7f280"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"actio