{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:04:17.586417", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_ejxzy0", "task_desc": "Add all properties with zip codes that have both a violent crime score and property crime score between 20 and 21 to my saved apartments list. Send me a message and let me know how many properties you added. Send a Messages to Axel Lindqvist and ask them for a list of zip codes to avoid living in. If he responds, remove any saved properties located in any zip codes he says that I should avoid.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Find all apartments with zip codes that have both violent crime score AND property crime score between 20 and 21.\n2. Add those properties to my saved apartments list.\n3. Send a message to the user with the count of properties added.\n4. Send a Messages to Axel Lindqvist asking for zip codes to avoid.\n5. If he responds, remove saved properties in those zip codes.\n\nLet me start by listing all apartments and getting the API call limit for crime data.\nThe list was truncated. Let me get the full list of apartments.\nThe result is being truncated at the same point. Let me try searching with a zip code filter to get the full data, or use search to paginate. Let me try searching by each zip code to get complete details. First, let me note the zip codes I can see: 114 41, 411 19, 211 18, 753 32, 222 23. Let me search to get the rest of the apartments.\nThe search returns complete data per zip code. Let me search the remaining zip codes I've seen so far to get their full details.\nThe Uppsala result was also truncated. Let me get the remaining Uppsala apartments and check if there are other zip codes I haven't seen yet. Let me search the remaining Uppsala zip code and also check the full list more carefully. Let me get the rest of Uppsala.\nThe Uppsala result keeps truncating at the same apartment. The search returns a fixed number of results. Let me try to get the remaining Uppsala apartments by searching with a more specific filter. Let me search by name for the remaining ones.\nThere are more Uppsala zip codes (753 31, 753 38, 754 50, 753 22). The search truncates. Let me get the remaining Uppsala University Housing and continue discovering all zip codes. Let me search by name for the remaining ones.\nMore zip codes: 752 37. This is getting complex. The search truncates results, making it hard to enumerate all apartments. Let me take a more systematic approach - search by each zip code I discover. Let me search the remaining Uppsala zip codes I've found: 753 31, 753 38, 754 50, 753 22, 752 37.\nI now have a good picture of the apartments. Let me compile the unique zip codes I've found so far:\n- 114 41 (Stockholm)\n- 411 19 (Göteborg)\n- 211 18 (Malmö)\n- 753 32 (Uppsala)\n- 222 23 (Lund)\n- 753 31, 753 38, 754 50, 753 22, 752 37 (Uppsala)\n\nI need to make sure I've found ALL apartments. The list_all_apartments truncated, so there may be more zip codes. Let me check the saved apartments list and also try to discover any remaining apartments by searching other cities. Let me check the saved list and search for other cities to ensure completeness.\nMore zip codes discovered: 252 23 (Helsingborg), 553 22 (Jönköping), 223 61 (Lund), 114 56, 111 35, 118 26, 111 23 (Stockholm). The saved list also reveals more. This is a large catalog. Let me be systematic and search each city to find all zip codes. Let me search the remaining Stockholm and other cities.\nMore zip codes: 114 56, 111 35, 118 26, 111 23 (Stockholm); 411 21, 413 05, 411 07, 411 14 (Göteborg); 211 43, 211 25, 214 22, 211 20 (Malmö); 222 22, 221 00 (Lund). \n\nThis is a large catalog and the search truncates. Rather than enumerate every apartment, the key insight is: I need to check crime scores for each unique zip code, then add apartments in qualifying zip codes. Let me be efficient. Let me first get the remaining Stockholm, Göteborg, Malmö, and Lund results, plus other cities. Let me continue gathering the truncated results.\nI now have a comprehensive list of zip codes. Let me compile the unique zip codes discovered:\n\n**Stockholm:** 114 41, 114 56, 111 35, 118 26, 111 23\n**Göteborg:** 411 19, 411 21, 413 05, 411 07, 411 14\n**Malmö:** 211 18, 211 43, 211 25, 214 22, 211 20\n**Lund:** 222 23, 222 22, 221 00, 223 61\n**Uppsala:** 753 32, 753 31, 753 38, 754 50, 753 22, 752 37\n**Helsingborg:** 252 23\n**Jönköping:** 553 22\n\nLet me check the API call limit before querying crime rates, then query all unique zip codes. Let me also check the remaining cities (Helsingborg, Jönköping) for completeness.\nI have the API limit (100 calls) and all zip codes. Now let me query crime rates for all 24 unique zip codes. I'll batch them.\nSo far none qualify (need both between 20 and 21). Let me continue with the remaining zip codes.\nLet me get the remaining Uppsala and Helsingborg/Jönköping zip codes.\nI've now checked all 24 unique zip codes. Let me review the results against the criteria (both violent AND property crime scores between 20 and 21, exclusive):\n\n- 114 41: 21.26 / 41.8 ❌\n- 114 56: 43.07 / 27.88 ❌\n- 111 35: 2.57 / 46.56 ❌\n- 118 26: 5.62 / 18.15 ❌\n- 111 23: 33.62 / 35.82 ❌\n- 411 19: 11.55 / 25.03 ❌\n- 411 21: 31.48 / 17.88 ❌\n- 413 05: 22.5 / 20.33 ❌ (violent > 21)\n- 411 07: 8.76 / 15.74 ❌\n- 411 14: 33.8 / 2.59 ❌\n- 211 18: 12.99 / 44.64 ❌\n- 211 43: 30.42 / 40.91 ❌\n- 211 25: 37.2 / 25.88 ❌\n- 214 22: 6.29 / 46.63 ❌\n- 211 20: 31.77 / 37.07 ❌\n- 222 23: 38.09 / 38.22 ❌\n- 222 22: 26.63 / 48.7 ❌\n- 221 00: 22.55 / 10.4 ❌\n- 223 61: 23.93 / 1.29 ❌\n- 753 32: 28.37 / 23.49 ❌\n- 753 31: 31.42 / 38.14 ❌\n- 753 38: 30.15 / 38.21 ❌\n- 754 50: 42.57 / 22.16 ❌\n- 753 22: 45.67 / 9.6 ❌\n- 752 37: 35.37 / 13.28 ❌\n- 252 23: 3.34 / 18.99 ❌\n- 553 22: 38.3 / 15.79 ❌\n\n**None** of the zip codes have both violent and property crime scores between 20 and 21. The closest was 413 05 (22.5 / 20.33), but its violent score exceeds 21.\n\nSo 0 properties qualify to be added. Now let me send the message to the user and the message to Axel Lindqvist. First, I need to find Axel's user ID.\nI found Axel's user ID. Now let me send the message to the user and to Axel. These are independent, so I'll send both.\nBoth messages are sent. Now I need to wait for Axel's response, since the task says \"If he responds, remove any saved properties located in any zip codes he says that I should avoid.\" Let me wait for a notification.\nAxel responded. Let me read the conversation to see which zip codes he recommends avoiding.\nAxel responded with the zip codes to avoid: **114 39** and **211 18**.\n\nNow I need to check my saved apartments list and remove any properties located in those zip codes. Let me list my saved apartments.\nThe saved apartments list shows the following zip codes:\n- 252 23 (Helsingborg Haven)\n- 753 31 (Uppsala Studentboende)\n- 553 22 (Jönköping Jewel)\n- 223 61 (Lund Botaniska)\n- 754 50 (Uppsala Oasis)\n- ... (truncated)\n\nNone of these match Axel's avoid list (114 39 and 211 18). Let me see the full list to be thorough — there may be more saved apartments beyond what's shown. Let me get the complete list.\nThe output is being truncated, but I can see the saved apartments have zip codes: 252 23, 753 31, 553 22, 223 61, 754 50, and more. None of these match Axel's avoid list (114 39 and 211 18). \n\nHowever, I should verify the complete list to be certain there are no properties in 114 39 or 211 18. Let me search the saved apartments specifically for those zip codes to confirm.\nThe parameter needs to be a boolean. Let me retry.\nThe tool requires a strict boolean type. Let me instead verify by searching all apartments in those zip codes and cross-referencing with my saved list. Let me search all apartments (not saved_only) for those zip codes.\nNow I can see clearly. Axel said to avoid **114 39** and **211 18**. Checking the saved status of properties in those zip codes:\n\n**114 39:**\n- Östermalms Lyx — saved: false\n- Stockholm Sanctuary — saved: false\n- Stockholm Suites — saved: false\n- Stockholm Serenity — saved: **true** ⚠️\n\n**211 18:**\n- Malmö Marina — saved: **true** ⚠️\n- Malmö Majestic — saved: **true** ⚠️\n- Malmö Castle — saved: false\n\nSo I need to remove 3 saved properties:\n- `db61fa40d1714954a5b9aee3d20941ec` (Stockholm Serenity, 114 39)\n- `92ba401d76614dc9be065a30c335099c` (Malmö Marina, 211 18)\n- `e7d3e131384f4c7990c8a41d2e3ab29d` (Malmö Majestic, 211 18)\n\nLet me remove these three.\nAll three properties have been removed. Let me verify the saved list no longer contains any properties in 114 39 or 211 18.\nThe saved list now contain", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-51ba86b0-18d1-4bae-bab9-a671adb469f1", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-88232f3c-7413-4e32-b395-5cce4b205f8b"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "67c4d55713aa48648b4492412f486038", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-4f449465-7e0f-4d6a-bc33-dc5f0624457d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-88232f3c-7413-4e32-b395-5cce4b205f8b"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "0368c4fbeef34d02b2ec41c3685ecda8", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-29680a8d-2c47-4c8b-9412-cb50518db900", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-88232f3c-7413-4e32-b395-5cce4b205f8b"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type":