\nWhat are your top 5 biceps exercises?\n\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.5, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "execution", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 514, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.7, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 1214.19, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1214.19, "prof_tok_in": 230600, "prof_tok_out": 2203, "prof_llm_calls": 13}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:14:24.065781", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_a6n7ro", "task_desc": "Find the address for the Malmö Opera, I took a cab there once. Schedule a van ride to pick me up from my  vacation house in Malmö, located at Norra Vallgatan 62, 211 22 Malmö, to the Malmö Opera on 10/19/2024 at 6 pm. Also, add \"Night at the Opera\" to the calendar for 10/19/2024 from 7 pm - 11 pm at Malmö Opera. Email Vasco the details about the event and let him know the cab ride will be picking us up at my house. Delete all my events for today as well. This is supposed to be a special night, a", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Find the address for the Malmö Opera, I took a cab there once. Schedule a van ride to pick me up from my  vacation house in Malmö, located at Norra Va\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll work through this task step by step. Let me start by gathering the information I need.\n\nLet me first find the Malmö Opera address and check my cab ride his\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll work through this task step by step. Let me start by gathering information about the Malmö Opera address from my cab ride history, and check today's calendar events.\nThe ride history needs an integer offset. Let me retry with proper types.\nThe tool seems to require integer types but is receiving strings. Let me try without specifying offset/limit.\nThere are 30 rides. Let me try retrieving them with integer-style calls. The issue is the parameter serialization. Let me try a different approach.\nThe tool is rejecting string arguments for integer parameters. Let me try passing the value without quotes in a way that may be interpreted as an integer.\nThe integer parameter validation is failing regardless. Let me try the search-based approach to find the Malmö Opera address instead. First, let me check the current user details and try to find the address through other means.\nThe ride history tool has a type bug, but I can find the Malmö Opera address through the cab service. The `list_rides` confirms the route exists between \"Norra Vallgatan 62, 211 22 Malmö\" and \"Malmö Opera\". Let me get the exact address of the Malmö Opera by getting a quotation, which may return the resolved address.\nThe cab service recognizes \"Malmö Opera\" as a valid destination. Let me try to get the precise street address by searching the web isn't available, but I can check if there's a contacts entry or other record. Let me search contacts and the calendar for the Malmö Opera address.\nNo contacts or calendar entries with the address. The cab service uses \"Malmö Opera\" as the canonical destination name. Let me try to retrieve the ride history one more time with a different approach to find the exact address from the user's past cab ride. Let me try the get_ride_history with the limit only.\nThe ride history tool consistently rejects integer parameters due to a type validation bug in this environment. I cannot retrieve the past ride's exact street address through that tool.\n\nHowever, I have strong confirmation that \"Malmö Opera\" is the recognized destination name in the cab system, and the route from the user's vacation house works. The Malmö Opera's well-known address is \"Östra Rönneholmsvägen 20, 211 47 Malmö\" — but I should not guess. Let me try one more time to access the ride history with a workaround, and also check if there's a saved location anywhere.\n\nLet me reconsider: the task says \"I took a cab there once\" — implying the address is in ride history. Since that tool is broken, I'll proceed using \"Malmö Opera\" as the destination (which the cab system resolves), but I should clarify the exact street address with the user since I cannot retrieve it.\n\nActually, let me first complete the actions I'm confident about, then clarify the address point. Let me proceed with the van ride booking, calendar event, and email — but I need the address for the email details. Let me try the ride history tool once more with a JSON integer.\nThe ride history tool is definitively broken for integer parameters in this environment. I cannot retrieve the exact street address from the past cab ride.\n\nGiven the user explicitly said \"This is supposed to be a special night, and I'm concerned about your not getting this right. Clarify with me if you're unsure about anything\" — and I am genuinely unsure about the exact street address of the Malmö Opera (the cab system only resolves it as \"Malmö Opera\"), I should clarify this one point before finalizing. But I can still proceed with the actions that don't depend on the exact address, and confirm the rest.\n\nLet me think about what I can confidently do:\n1. ✅ Van ride from Norra Vallgatan 62 to Malmö Opera on 10/19/2024 6pm — the cab system resolves \"Malmö Opera\"\n2. ✅ Calendar event \"Night at the Opera\" 10/19 7-11pm at Malmö Opera\n3. ✅ Delete today's events (3 events)\n4. ⚠️ Email Vasco — needs his contact info and the address detail\n5. ❓ Exact street address of Malmö Opera — cannot retrieve from broken ride history\n\nLet me get Vasco's contact info and proceed with the confident actions. Let me also try to find Vasco.\nThe van ride is booked and the calendar event is created. Now I have a problem: there are **three** contacts named \"Vasco\" (Martins, Pinto, Pereira). I'm unsure which one is the intended recipient. The user said \"Email Vasco\" without specifying.\n\nLet me also note: I still cannot retrieve the exact street address of the Malmö Opera from the broken ride history tool.\n\nGiven the user's explicit instruction to clarify when unsure, I have two genuine uncertainties:\n1. **Which Vasco** should receive the email (3 candidates)\n2. **The exact street address** of the Malmö Opera (cab system only resolves \"Malmö Opera\"; ride history tool is broken)\n\nLet me delete today's events first (that's unambiguous), then clarify with the user.\nAll three of today's events are deleted. Now I have two genuine uncertainties that I should clarify with the user before sending the email, per their explicit request to clarify when unsure:\n\n1. **Which Vasco?** There are three contacts named Vasco:\n   - Vasco Martins (vmartins@gaia2mail.com) — retired professor, Lisbon\n   - Vasco Pinto (vascopinto70@gaia2mail.com) — retired teacher, Porto\n   - Vasco Pereira (mechanical engineer, Porto)\n\n2. **The exact street address of the Malmö Opera** — The cab ride history tool is broken (it rejects integer parameters with a type error), so I couldn't pull the exact address from your past cab ride. The cab system recognizes the destination simply as \"Malmö Opera.\"\n\nLet me clarify these with the user before sending the email.\nI've sent the clarification to the user. I'll wait for their response before sending the email, since I have two genuine uncertainties (which Vasco to email, and the exact street address of the Malmö Opera).\nNo response yet after waiting. Let me wait a bit longer for the user's clarification.\nStill no response from the user after waiting a total of 10 minutes. I've completed all the unambiguous parts of the task and have clearly flagged the two items I need clarification on. Let me do a final check of the current state to confirm everything is in order, then summarize.\n\nLet me verify the calendar state and the booked ride.\nEverything is confirmed in place. Let me provide a final summary to the user. I've completed all the unambiguous actions and am awaiting their clarification on the two open items before sending the email.\nI've completed all the unambiguous parts of the task and clearly flagged the two items requiring clarification, exactly as the user requested (\"Clarify with me if you're unsure about anything\").\n\n**Summary of what's done:**\n- ✅ Booked the **Van** ride from Norra Vallgatan 62, 211 22 Malmö → Malmö Opera on 10/19/2024 at 6:00 PM\n- ✅ Added the **\"Night at the Opera\"** calendar event (10/19/2024, 7–11 PM at Malmö Opera)\n- ✅ Deleted all 3 of today's events\n\n**Awaiting user clarification on two genuine uncertainties before I can send the email to Vasco:**\n1. **Which Vasco** — there are three contacts with that name (Martins, Pinto, Pereira)\n2. **The exact street address of the Malmö Opera** — the cab ride-history tool is broken (returns a type error on integer parameters), so I couldn't retrieve the address from the user's past cab ride; the cab system only resolves the destination as \"Malmö Opera\"\n\nI'll send the email to the correct Vasco with the full details (including the house pickup) as soon as the user replies.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-0f009f67-5db9-45ca-a93a-d8930d451233", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f55bfb57-6795-4539-bff0-ab231b9d96c9"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Night at the Opera", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 19:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 23:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "Malmö Opera", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-9acec066-ba26-4765-b477-c11d567c172f", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f55bfb57-6795-4539-bff0-ab231b9d96c9"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "d2f892cf34ab4e16be08eb6dbfd01727", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-be9bca64-b622-440e-b1a4-0f5bf145acea", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f55bfb57-6795-4539-bff0-ab231b9d96c9"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "541223c32f0b40edb923a728928ace2c", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-b60a4ce0-0ab7-41ca-affb-b06e3173135d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f55bfb57-6795-4539-bff0-ab231b9d96c9"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "9daa4008ccb14c48a7fd156b953b5c3a", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-40310719-6268-4e6d-b349-4e5e192c082d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f55bfb57-6795-4539-bff0-ab231b9d96c9"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "order_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "start_location", "value": "Norra Vallgatan 62, 211 22 Malmö", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_location", "value": "Malmö Opera, 211 18 Malmö", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "service_type", "value": "Van", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "ride_time", "value": "2024-10-19 18:00:00", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-bbbba111-595c-49c9-a5a9-be54638d3a12", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f55bfb57-6795-