{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:14:42.363880", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_4o5b3h", "task_desc": "Send a Messages message to Axel in my one-on-one conversation with him asking if he still wants to meet for coffee as I haven't received a calendar invite from him yet, and invite him to join me on this Friday at 2:00pm at the Coffee Shop located at Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm. Set up the event in my calendar for an hour on that day and name it \"Coffee Break with Axel\". Book a default cab to pick me up 30 minutes ahead of our coffee break from Home to the Coffee Shop. Let me know when y", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Send a Messages message to Axel in my one-on-one conversation with him asking if he still wants to meet for coffee as I haven't received a calendar in\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by gathering the information I need: finding Axel's contact info, checking my calendar for Friday, and understanding the current state. Let me make s\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by gathering the information I need: finding Axel's contact info, checking my calendar for Friday, and understanding the current state. Let me make several independent calls.\nI found Axel's contact (Axel Lindqvist, +46202123456). Today is Tuesday, 2024-10-15, so this Friday is 2024-10-18. Let me check my one-on-one conversation with Axel and look at Friday's calendar to confirm availability.\nI see two conversations with Axel. The first is a group conversation (3 participants). The second appears to be a one-on-one with Axel and +46734567890 (Astrid). Let me read the second conversation fully to confirm it's my one-on-one with Axel.\nThis conversation (d9e8aed8d70c46e3a22eea360f8328f2) is a group with +46734567890 (Astrid), +46181234567, and +46202123456 (Axel) — not a one-on-one. Let me read the second conversation to find my actual one-on-one with Axel.\nLet me retry with integer offset.\nThe tool seems to require integer but the schema passes string. Let me try without offset, or use get_existing_conversation_ids to find the one-on-one conversation with just me and Axel.\nThere's a one-on-one conversation with Axel: `bd5fd1ae6f9947dda2e6631c4cde1773`. Let me read it to confirm and see the context.\nThis is my one-on-one conversation with Axel (the other participant is +46734567890, which is me — the current user). I can see Axel mentioned he'd \"send you a calendar invite for next week\" but I haven't received one. \n\nNow let me proceed with the 3 tasks. First, let me send the message to Axel, set up the calendar event, and book the cab. These are independent actions, so I'll do them together.\n\nFriday is 2024-10-18. Coffee break: 14:00–15:00. Cab pickup 30 min ahead = 13:30 from Home to Coffee Shop.\nAll 3 tasks are done:\n1. ✅ Message sent to Axel in our one-on-one conversation\n2. ✅ Calendar event \"Coffee Break with Axel\" created for Friday 2024-10-18, 14:00–15:00\n3. ✅ Default cab booked from Home to the Coffee Shop at 13:30 (30 min before)\n\nNow I need to handle the conditional: \"If Axel is not available, reschedule...\" and \"If anyone else sends me a Messages message with an invite to an event, please ignore them.\" I should wait for any follow-up notifications (e.g., Axel replying about availability, or others sending invites). Let me wait for notifications.\nThere are new messages. One is in my one-on-one conversation with Axel (bd5fd1ae6f9947dda2e6631c4cde1773) — this could be his availability reply. The other two (c70dd0c5720e44b4a02e725661239284 and ca0fc7c4f01f4a6ca44a329ac3836633) are from other conversations — possibly event invites from others, which I should ignore. Let me read the Axel conversation to check his reply.\nAxel replied: he's NOT available on Friday, but is available the following Monday or Tuesday at 2:00pm. The task says: \"If Axel is not available, reschedule our Coffee Break for the earliest day that we are both available.\"\n\nThe earliest day Axel is available is the following Monday. Today is Tuesday 2024-10-15, so \"the following Monday\" = 2024-10-21. I need to verify I'm also available that Monday at 2:00pm. Let me check my calendar for Monday 2024-10-21 and Tuesday 2024-10-22.\nAnalysis of availability:\n- **Monday 2024-10-21**: I have Content Creation (10:00–12:00) and Yoga (18:00–19:00). At 2:00pm I'm FREE. ✅\n- **Tuesday 2024-10-22**: I have Brand Partnership Meeting (14:00–16:00) — conflicts with 2:00pm. ❌\n\nSo the earliest day we are BOTH available is **Monday, 2024-10-21 at 2:00pm**. \n\nNow I need to:\n1. Reschedule the calendar event from Friday to Monday 2024-10-21, 14:00–15:00\n2. Rebook the cab for 13:30 on Monday 2024-10-21\n3. Reply to Axel confirming the new date\n\nLet me first delete the old calendar event and cancel the old cab, then create the new ones. Let me delete the Friday event and cancel the Friday cab.\nNow let me create the rescheduled calendar event for Monday 2024-10-21, 14:00–15:00, and book the new cab for 13:30 that day.\nNow let me reply to Axel confirming the new date (Monday 2024-10-21 at 2:00pm).\nNow, regarding the other two new messages (conversation IDs c70dd0c5720e44b4a02e725661239284 and ca0fc7c4f01f4a6ca44a329ac3836633) — the task says to ignore anyone else who sends me a Messages message with an invite to an event, and that the user will reply later. I should not act on those. But let me quickly verify they are indeed event invites from others (not Axel) so I'm confident in ignoring them. Let me check them briefly.\nConfirmed: Both other new messages are event invites from other people (Beshoy +4531123458 inviting me to coffee next Wednesday, and Nomsa +33612345678 inviting me to an anniversary gathering). Per the task instructions, I will ignore these and let the user reply later.\n\nAll tasks are now complete. Let me summarize what was done and notify the user.\n\nSummary of actions taken:\n1. **Message to Axel** (one-on-one conversation): Asked if he still wants to meet for coffee since I hadn't received his calendar invite, and invited him to Friday at 2:00pm at the Coffee Shop.\n2. **Calendar event**: Created \"Coffee Break with Axel\" for Friday 2024-10-18 14:00–15:00.\n3. **Cab**: Booked a Default cab from Home to the Coffee Shop at 13:30 (30 min before).\n\nThen Axel replied he's **not available Friday** but available Monday or Tuesday at 2:00pm. So I:\n- Deleted the Friday event, created a new one for **Monday 2024-10-21 14:00–15:00** (earliest day we're both free — Tuesday had a conflict at 2pm).\n- Cancelled the Friday cab, rebooked for **Monday 2024-10-21 13:30**.\n- Replied to Axel confirming Monday Oct 21 at 2:00pm.\n\nI also ignored two event-invite messages from other people (Beshoy and Nomsa) as instructed.\nThe task is fully complete. All sub-requests have been handled:\n\n1. ✅ Sent the message to Axel in our one-on-one conversation\n2. ✅ Created the \"Coffee Break with Axel\" calendar event\n3. ✅ Booked the Default cab 30 minutes ahead\n4. ✅ Since Axel was unavailable Friday, rescheduled to the earliest mutually available day (Monday Oct 21, as Tuesday had a conflict), rebooked the cab, and confirmed the new date with Axel\n5. ✅ Ignored the two event-invite messages from other people as instructed\n\nI've notified the user of everything that was done.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a2da3f6f-4d4e-4100-9db7-c9398d589afc", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-20c3836c-4d47-445c-b1a3-94851d8e8a80"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46202123456", "value_type": "