{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:14:42.364368", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_72o73s", "task_desc": "Delete that guy Kasper from my contacts list, we had a falling out. Additionally, delete all the events with two attendees (including myself, even if I'm not explicitly listed), scheduled from the 1st through the 4th of next month. Send a group email to all the attendees of the canceled events explaining to them that I won't be able to attend any events in that period.\nSend an email to a film producer who lives in Stockholm telling him that I will be free the first day of next month to discuss t", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n\n1. Delete contact \"Kasper\" from contacts\n2. Delete all events with 2 attendees (including myself) scheduled Nov 1-4, 2024\n3. Send group email to all attendees of canceled events explaining I can't attend\n4. Send email to a film producer in Stockholm about being free Nov 1\n5. Schedule \"Short Film\" event Nov 1, 9AM-7PM at Multiproduktion Norden AB\n6. Order 2 units of most expensive black Batman filmcells\n\nLet me start by gathering information in parallel.\nI found two Kasper contacts. The task says \"that guy Kasper\" - I need to determine which one. Let me also note the events query got cut off. Let me get more details.\n\nThe Stockholm search returned nothing in contacts. Let me search differently for the film producer, and get the full events list. The events list was truncated - I need to see all events from Nov 1-4. Let me also check which Kasper is relevant.\n\nLet me gather more info:\nI found the film producer: Åke Lindström, Film Producer in Stockholm. \n\nThe events query had a type error with offset as string. Let me retry with integer offset, and the shopping list also had an issue. Let me retry both.\nThe tools are rejecting string arguments for offset/limit. Let me try without those parameters (using defaults).\nThe events list is truncated (showing only 5 events, last one cut off). The shopping list has 500 products and these aren't filmcells. Let me search for the Batman filmcells product properly and get the full events list. The events query seems to have a default limit of 10 but returned truncated. Let me search events by tag/title and search shopping for Batman.\n\nLet me search for the Batman filmcells product and get all events in the range. The events list appears truncated at \"Ast\" - I need to see the full list. Let me use search_events to find events, and search the shopping product.\nThe search_events returns all events (not just the date range). I need to focus on Nov 1-4 events. The Batman filmcells product is \"Filmcells Batman Begins Minicell Framed Art, S2\" with variants. The black color variant is item_id \"7d584c2f680642c48e04d70032b0e9da\" at $59.03 (available). But there's also a more expensive black option? Let me check - the black ones are $59.03 (available) and $54.99 (unavailable). The most expensive black available is $59.03.\n\nWait, I need to find the MOST EXPENSIVE Batman filmcells in black. Let me check if there are other Batman filmcells products. The search returned multiple Batman items. Let me get details on the filmcells product and also check the other Batman items. But first, let me get the complete list of Nov 1-4 events. The get_calendar_events_from_to returned truncated data. Let me try reading each event. Actually, the issue is the response was truncated in display. Let me re-call it - it returned 5 events but the 5th was cut off. There may be more events beyond what's shown.\n\nLet me get the full events list for the range by reading individual events. Actually, the truncation is just in the tool result display. Let me re-call get_calendar_events_from_to to see if I can get the complete list. The default limit might be 10. Let me try a different approach - search for specific dates.\n\nActually, the result showed events but got cut at \"Ast\" for the 5th event. There could be more. Let me re-request and see the full output.\nThe result is consistently truncated at the 5th event (\"Dinner with Axel\"). This appears to be a display truncation issue. The 5th event \"Dinner with Axel\" has attendees starting with \"Ast\" (likely \"Astrid Lundqvist\" + \"Axel Lindqvist\" = 2 attendees). There may be more events after this. Let me try to get events for each day separately to see the complete picture, and also check Nov 3-4 specifically.\nNow I have a clearer picture. Let me compile the Nov 1-4 events:\n\n**Nov 1:**\n1. Meeting with Jiaying - attendees: Astrid Lundqvist, Jiaying Liang (2) ✓\n2. Coffee Break with João - attendees: Astrid Lundqvist, João Pereira (2) ✓\n3. Networking Event - attendees: Astrid Lundqvist, Luísa Silva e Sousa (2) ✓\n\n**Nov 2:**\n4. Event Planning Meeting - attendees: Astrid Lundqvist, Astrid Svensson (2) ✓\n5. Dinner with Axel - attendees: Astrid Lundqvist, Axel Lindqvist (2) ✓\n\n**Nov 3:**\n6. Self-Care Sunday - attendees: Astrid Lundqvist (1) ✗ (only me)\n\n**Nov 4:**\n7. Influencer Meeting with Åke Svensson - attendees: Åke Svensson (1) ✗ (not me)\n8. Yoga Class - attendees: [] (0) ✗\n9. Content Creation - attendees: [] (0) ✗\n\nThe task says \"events with two attendees (including myself, even if I'm not explicitly listed)\". So I need events where total attendees = 2, counting myself. Events 1-5 all have exactly 2 attendees including Astrid (me). Events 6-9 don't qualify (1 or 0 attendees, and I'm not in 7-9).\n\nSo I need to delete events 1-5. The attendees of canceled events (excluding myself) are: Jiaying Liang, João Pereira, Luísa Silva e Sousa, Astrid Svensson, Axel Lindqvist.\n\nLet me verify the current user is Astrid Lundqvist, and get the full attendee list. Let me also confirm the Batman filmcells details. Let me proceed with deletions and verify user.\nConfirmed. Current user is Astrid Lundqvist. The 5 events to delete (each with exactly 2 attendees including me):\n1. Meeting with Jiaying (Jiaying Liang)\n2. Coffee Break with João (João Pereira)\n3. Networking Event (Luísa Silva e Sousa)\n4. Event Planning Meeting (Astrid Svensson)\n5. Dinner with Axel (Axel Lindqvist)\n\nNow let me delete these 5 events and delete the Kasper contact. There are two Kaspers - the task says \"that guy Kasper\" with a falling out. I'll need to decide. Let me think: the task is ambiguous between two Kaspers. However, I should pick the one most likely. Both are Danish. Without more context, I cannot definitively know which. But the task says \"that guy Kasper\" implying a specific known one. \n\nGiven ambiguity, I should ask the user. But the instructions say to complete the task. Let me reconsider - perhaps I should delete both? No, that could be wrong. Let me ask the user to clarify which Kasper, since deleting the wrong contact is irreversible and harmful.\n\nActually, let me first do the clearly-defined actions (delete events, schedule, order, emails) and clarify the Kasper ambiguity. But the task bundles everything. Let me delete the 5 events now (clear), and ask about Kasper.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the Kasper issue. The two contacts:\n- Kasper Rasmussen: High School Teacher, Aarhus\n- Kasper Mikkelsen: Software Engineer, Copenhagen\n\nNeither has obvious \"falling out\" context. I'll ask the user which one to delete to avoid a mistake. But first, let me complete the unambiguous parts. Let me delete the 5 events now.\nAll 5 events deleted. Now I need to handle the Kasper ambiguity. There are two Kasper contacts. Let me ask the user which one to delete, since this is irreversible and the task is ambiguous. Meanwhile, let me proceed with the other clearly-defined tasks.\n\nLet me first get the attendee emails for the group email. I need emails for: Jiaying Liang, João Pereira, Luísa Silva e Sousa, Astrid Svensson, Axel Lindqvist. Let me search contacts for these. Also let me get the Batman filmcells product details to confirm the most expensive black variant.\n\nLet me ask the user about Kasper and gather attendee info in parallel.\nI have most attendee emails. Note: the \"Luísa Silva e Sousa\" from the event doesn't exactly match the contacts found (those are Luísa Figueiredo and Maria Luísa Sousa e Silva). The event attendee \"Luísa Silva e Sousa\" may not have a contact entry. Let me search more specifically for \"Silva e Sousa\" and \"Luísa Silva\". Also I need João Pereira's email (jpereira@fc.ul.pt - found). \n\nFor the Batman filmcells: the black color variants are $59.03 (available, item 7d584c2f...) and $54.99 (unavailable). The most expensive AVAILABLE black one is $59.03. The task says \"most expensive Batman filmcells in black color\" - I'll use the available black one at $59.03 (the $54.99 black is unavailable).\n\nLet ", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-9b193428-998f-4eed-8d54-59c607b1cd18", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9219b53f-1c0e-48ca-9831-ffd7e044eaa8"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "2e3244344b89404bad46a6a207a3afd3", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a1ececd0-e152-4368-aae3-d5e68ae62ceb", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9219b53f-1c0e-48ca-9831-ffd7e044eaa8"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "63241d3ef22e49e4a9f92744c4af1a5b", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-3cb0bfd9-92d2-4a3e-93fa-24912fbf5ba8", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9219b53f-1c0e-48ca-98