{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:19:14.405922", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_1afh09", "task_desc": "Please tell me the average age of the people in my contacts who live in the city that appears most frequently among my contacts (if there is a tie, sort alphabetically and use the first one) considering only those who have ever emailed me. Round to the nearest whole number.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Please tell me the average age of the people in my contacts who live in the city that appears most frequently among my contacts (if there is a tie, so\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into steps:\n1. Find contacts who have ever emailed me (check emails)\n2. Among those, find the city that appears most frequently (tie → alph\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll break this task into steps:\n1. Get all my contacts (with their city and age)\n2. Determine which contacts have ever emailed me\n3. Find the most frequent city among those contacts (tie → alphabetical first)\n4. Compute the average age of those contacts in that city, rounded to nearest whole number\n\nLet me start by gathering contacts and emails.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nThe tool seems to be rejecting the string \"0\". Let me try without the offset parameter (using default).\nThe contacts and emails are paginated. Let me get more contacts (with offset) and more emails. The offset parameter seems to need an integer but the tool rejected \"0\" as string. Let me try passing offset as a number without quotes by using the parameter differently. Actually the issue is the tool received a string. Let me try listing more emails and contacts by scrolling.\n\nLet me get the next page of contacts and emails.\nThe offset parameter is being passed as a string. Let me try a different approach - perhaps the tool accepts offset when I don't quote it. Let me try with the value as a bare number.\nThe tool keeps rejecting the offset. Let me check if there's a view limit by getting contacts without offset again - maybe it returns all contacts at once, or maybe I need to find another way. Let me try the search_contacts approach or check how many contacts there are. Let me first try listing emails without offset to see the full inbox, and try get_contacts again to see if it paginates differently.\n\nActually, the first call without offset returned 2 contacts. There may be a view limit of 2. Let me try a much larger offset value to see if it's a parsing issue, or try the InternalContacts tool which might behave differently.\nBoth contact tools return only 2 contacts (view limit of 2) and reject offset. The emails list also rejects offset. I need another way to enumerate all contacts and emails.\n\nFor contacts, I can use search_contacts with different queries to find more. But that's inefficient. Let me think - the view limit is 2. Maybe I can search contacts by partial name matches. But I don't know all names.\n\nFor emails, the list_emails rejects offset too. But I can use search_emails to find emails. However, I need to know which contacts emailed me.\n\nLet me try a different approach for emails - maybe search_emails works. And for contacts, let me try search_contacts with common letters. Actually, let me first try search_emails to see if it works, and try get_contacts with various offsets using integer-like values.\n\nLet me try search_emails and search_contacts.\nThe search tools also return only 2 results (the view limit). The search_emails with \"@\" returned 2 emails. The search_contacts with \"a\" returned 2 contacts.\n\nThe view limit is 2 per call. I need to find a way to enumerate all. The search returns partial matches - maybe I can search with different queries to get different subsets. But that's unreliable.\n\nLet me reconsider. The offset parameter is being rejected as a string. This might be a quirk where I need to pass it differently. Let me try the offset as a number value (not in quotes) - in the function call format, maybe I should pass it without quotes. Let me try again carefully with offset as a bare integer.\n\nActually, the issue might be that the harness wraps all args as strings. Let me try a workaround: search_contacts with very specific queries to enumerate. But first, let me try get_contacts with offset passed as integer literal.\n\nLet me try the offset with different integer values to see if any work.\nThe offset is consistently rejected. The view limit is 2. I'll need to enumerate contacts and emails via search with different queries to cover all entries.\n\nFor contacts, search looks at first name, last name, phone, email. Let me try searching with different letters to find more contacts. Let me try several distinct queries in parallel.\n\nFor emails, search looks at sender, recipients, subject, content. The \"@\" search returned 2. Let me try searching with different terms.\n\nLet me try a batch of contact searches with different starting letters and email searches.\nThe search returns up to 2 results and seems to prioritize certain contacts. The \"e\" search revealed new contacts: Søren Kierkegaardsen (Copenhagen), Astrid Jensen (Copenhagen), Åke Lundqvist (Stockholm). The \"i\", \"o\", \"u\", \"m\" searches returned the same default 2.\n\nThis is tricky. The search returns only 2 results and seems to return the same top matches. I need a more systematic approach. Let me search by last name fragments and email domains to find more contacts. Let me try searching with distinctive substrings.\n\nLet me try searching with various letters that might appear in names to surface different contacts.\nThe search consistently returns the same top 3 contacts (Astrid Lundqvist, Søren Kierkegaardsen, Astrid Jensen) plus Jianhua Wang. The search seems to return a fixed set of \"top matches\" rather than all matches. This is a view-limited search.\n\nThe search returns up to 3 results now (it showed 3 for \"s\", \"r\", \"d\"). The results are dominated by Astrid Lundqvist, Søren, Astrid Jensen, Jianhua. These appear to be the highest-priority matches.\n\nI need a different strategy. The search returns partial matches but caps at a small number. Let me try searching with more specific/unique substrings that would match fewer contacts and reveal others. For example, searching by email domain fragments or specific last names.\n\nLet me try searching with distinctive substrings that might match other contacts not yet seen.\nNow I'm finding more contacts by searching specific substrings. New ones found:\n- Emil Rasmussen (Copenhagen, 21)\n- Lianying Wang (Beijing, 79)\n- Søren Jensen (Copenhagen, 60)\n\nThe search returns up to 3 results and seems to return the most relevant. I need to systematically find ALL contacts. Let me continue searching with distinctive terms. Let me search for more last names and email fragments.\nNew contacts found:\n- Astrid Rasmussen (Copenhagen, 30)\n- Kasper Rasmussen (Aarhus, 32)\n\nThe city searches returned nothing (search only matches name/phone/email, not city). Let me continue searching with more distinctive last names and email fragments to find remaining contacts.\nNew contact found:\n- Åsa Lundqvist (Stockholm, 79) - description cut off but city is Stockholm\n\nLet me get Åsa's full details and continue searching for more contacts. Let me search with more distinctive terms.\nÅsa Lundqvist is in Uppsala (79). The description-based searches (bakery, teacher) return nothing, confirming search only matches name/phone/email.\n\nSo far I have these contacts:\n1. Astrid Lundqvist (Stockholm, 23) - is_user\n2. Jianhua Wang (Shanghai, 68)\n3. Søren Kierkegaardsen (Copenhagen, 57)\n4. Astrid Jensen (Copenhagen, 31)\n5. Åke Lundqvist (Stockholm, 45)\n6. Emil Rasmussen (Copenhagen, 21)\n7. Lianying Wang (Beijing, 79)\n8. Søren Jensen (Copenhagen, 60)\n9. Astrid Rasmussen (Copenhagen, 30)\n10. Kasper Rasmussen (Aarhus, 32)\n11. Åsa Lundqvist (Uppsala, 79)\n\nI need to find if there are more contacts. Let me search with more distinctive first names and email fragments. Let me try various letters/names.\nMore contacts found:\n- Brother Mikael Svensson (Stockholm, 51)\n- Luís Pimentel (Porto, 45)\n- Aurélien Zylberberg (Paris, 61)\n- Luísa Figueiredo (Porto, 72)\n- Aurélie Dupont (Paris) - description cut off\n\nThe search returns up to 3 results. I need to keep finding more. Let me search with more letters and distinctive terms.\nMore contacts found:\n- Khurram Saeed (Lisbon, 70)\n- Wei Jianming (Shanghai, 50)\n- Vasco Martins (Lisbon, 74)\n\nThe search returns up to 3 results. I need to keep finding more. Let me search with more letters and distinctive terms.\nNew contact found:\n- Jiaqi Zhang (Shanghai, 23) - description cut off\n\nThe search returns up to 3 results. I need to keep finding more. Let me search with more letters and distinctive terms.\nThe search returns up to 3 results. I need to keep finding more. Let me se", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-f2c7e5dc-de18-4558-a9f8-89dd0ab106e4", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-7b52e176-2a52-4fdb-90af-e56733997b1f"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "45", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "search", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 646, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode":