{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:19:14.410661", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_0obld3", "task_desc": "In my Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, suggest the dates and times two hours before my next two yoga classes for a 1 hour call between the three of us. Let me know as soon as you’ve done this. Wait exactly 3 minutes from your message to me for responses. If availability is confirmed by both of them in that time, schedule the call at the agreed upon time. If they are both available for both times, tell them in the same Messages conversation that we'll do the earlier one. I", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: In my Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, suggest the dates and times two hours before my next two yoga classes for a 1 hour call\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by understanding the task. Let me break it down:\n\n1. Find my next two yoga classes (calendar)\n2. Calculate times two hours before each class\n3. Find \nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by understanding the task. Let me break it down:\n\n1. Find my next two yoga classes (calendar)\n2. Calculate times two hours before each class\n3. Find the Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne\n4. Suggest those two times for a 1-hour call\n5. Wait 3 minutes for responses\n6. Based on responses, schedule the call and confirm\n\nLet me begin by gathering the necessary information.\nThe search returned yoga classes but I need to find the \"next two\" relative to the current date. Let me check the current time and get the full list of yoga events. The search didn't find the conversation by that query, so let me search differently.\nThe current sim time is 1728975603 (2024-10-15). The yoga classes I've seen are all in August 2024, which are in the past. I need to find the next two yoga classes from the current date. Let me get the full list of Health events and also look at the conversations found. The conversation \"ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9\" appears in both searches, which is likely the one with both Joana and Vigdis.\n\nLet me get the full event list and read that conversation.\nThe conversation ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9 has participants +351954123456, +46734567890, +4571345678. Let me verify which is Joana and which is Vigdis, and fix the calendar query (limit must be int).\nConfirmed: +351954123456 = Joana Silva, +46734567890 = Astrid Lundqvist (me), +4571345678 = Vigdis Rønne. This is the right conversation.\n\nThe calendar query keeps failing on the limit type. Let me try without the limit parameter (it has a default).\nThis list shows events from 2024-10-15 onward but I don't see yoga classes yet. The list may be truncated. Let me search specifically for yoga events to find the next two.\nThe search results are truncated. I need to see all yoga classes to find the next two after 2024-10-15. Let me get the full event list by paginating through the date range. Let me try the from_to with a smaller explicit limit as int via a different approach, or get more events. Let me query a narrower future range and increase offset.\nThe tool is rejecting string-typed numeric arguments. Let me try passing them as actual integers (no quotes) in the JSON.\nThe tool seems to coerce all arguments to strings. The default limit is 10, which is why my earlier call returned only 10 events. Let me paginate using offset as a string but the issue is the type check. Let me try the default call again but it only returns 10. \n\nActually, the earlier successful call (without offset/limit) returned 10 events starting 2024-10-15. I need more. Let me try a different approach - query a future-only window that's small enough to fit in 10 results, e.g., a window that only contains yoga classes. But I don't know when they are.\n\nLet me try querying with offset omitted and just limit, to see if limit alone works as the default. Actually the default call returned 10. Let me try to get the next page by using a start date further out. First, let me see the full 10 results I got - they were truncated in display. Let me re-call and read carefully, then shift the window.\n\nLet me query a window starting later to find yoga classes. I'll try a window from 2024-10-20 onward.\nI found the first future yoga class: Monday, 2024-10-21 18:00:00 (event 23ff2e41249940288e488a0fb8f5a756). I need the second one. Let me query a window starting after this class to find the next yoga class.\nThis window shows events from 2024-10-22 but I need to find the next Yoga Class. The list is truncated at 10 events. Let me query a window starting after 2024-10-23 to find the next yoga class.\nStill no second yoga class in this window (truncated at 10). Let me continue shifting the window forward to find the next Yoga Class after 2024-10-21.\nI found the second future yoga class: Sunday, 2024-10-27 18:00:00 (event be936d6b1c3a4e5480a82e571fe84079).\n\nSo my next two yoga classes are:\n1. **Monday, 2024-10-21 18:00:00** → two hours before = **Monday, 2024-10-21 16:00:00**\n2. **Sunday, 2024-10-27 18:00:00** → two hours before = **Sunday, 2024-10-27 16:00:00**\n\nNow let me send the suggestion message to the conversation with Joana and Vigdis (ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9).\nI've sent the suggestion. Now I need to let the user know I've done this, then wait exactly 3 minutes for responses. Let me inform the user first.\nThere are new messages in the conversation. However, the task says to wait exactly 3 minutes from my message before checking responses. Let me wait 3 minutes (180 seconds) as instructed, then check the conversation.\n3 minutes have passed. Now let me read the conversation to check for responses from Joana and Vigdis.\nLet me analyze the responses within the 3-minute window (timestamps 1728975641, which is 2024-10-15 07:00:41, within 3 min of my 07:00:38 message):\n\n- **Joana (+351954123456)**: \"Both of those times are good for me!\" → available for BOTH times ✓\n- **Vigdis (+4571345678)**: \"Give me one second while I check my schedule!\" → NOT a confirmation. \"I'm up for 4-5PM on the 16th!\" → that's a different date (Oct 16), not either of my proposed options.\n\nSo Vigdis did NOT confirm availability for either of the two proposed times. Only Joana confirmed (for both). Since the task requires BOTH to confirm availability for the times to schedule, and Vigdis did not confirm either time, the condition \"availability is confirmed by both of them\" is NOT met.\n\nPer the task: \"If only one or neither of them replies, you're done.\" Vigdis replied but didn't confirm either proposed time, and only Joana confirmed. Both did not confirm availability for the proposed times, so I'm done — no scheduling, no confirmation message needed.\n\nLet me inform the user of the outcome.\nI've completed the task. Here's a summary of what happened:\n\n**Actions taken:**\n1. Found my next two yoga classes on the calendar:\n   - Monday, October 21 at 18:00\n   - Sunday, October 27 at 18:00\n2. Calculated the two proposed call times (2 hours before each): Monday Oct 21 at 16:00 and Sunday Oct 27 at 16:00.\n3. Sent the suggestion to the Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne.\n4. Let you know immediately, then waited exactly 3 minutes for responses.\n\n**Outcome after the 3-minute wait:**\n- Joana confirmed she's available for **both** times.\n- Vigdis did **not** confirm either proposed time (she said she'd check her schedule and instead suggested 4–5 PM on the 16th, a different date).\n\nSince both of them did not confirm availability for the proposed times, the scheduling condition wasn't met. Per your instructions, in that case I'm done — no call was scheduled and no confirmation message was sent. I've reported the result to you above.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-395097df-23ff-4689-a281-4b85f574d78d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-1002ac8b-cff9-409e-9170-a615155a24bb"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message_to_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "conversation_id", "value": "ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Joana and Vigdis, I was thinking of scheduling a 1-hour call with both of you. Would both of you be available on Oct 16 at 4 PM or Oct 17 at 4 PM? ", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-e18425b4-df03-4b0a-8777-ce4f314d566e", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-395097df-23ff-4689-a281-4b85f574d78d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Message sent to Joana and Vigdis suggesting a 1-hour call on October 16 at 4 PM and October 17 at 4 PM. Waiting for their response.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-81a7cc64-32f8-472d-a4cc-408a781c0d38", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-479d2a41-6896-4780-9f73-3dbc51784e01", "OracleEvent-AGENT-ded9b844-a686-4fe0-8313-baed17e87e8d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "October 16 at 4 PM was chosen as the date and time for the 1-hour call with Joana and Vigdis.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-479d2a41-6896-4780-9f73-3dbc51784e01", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-e53b14eb-4f75-4fed-912f-29b6acb98f7b", "Event-ENV-c2a86c3c-e49e-4beb-8156-fae9d918c57f"], "event_relative_time": 30.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Phone Call with Joana and Vigdis", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 16:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 17:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Joana Silva\",\"Vigdis Rønne\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-ded9b844-a686-4fe0-8313-baed17e87e8d", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-c2a86c3c-e49e-4beb-8156-fae9d918c57f", "Event-ENV-e53b14eb-4f75-4fed-912f-29b6acb98f7b"], "event_relative_time": 30.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message_to_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "conversation_id", "value": "ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Joana and Vigdis, just confirming our 1 hour call for October 16 at 4 PM. Looking forward to catching up then!", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.4, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "time", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 566, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 1298.41, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1298.41, "prof_tok_in": 395688, "prof_tok_out": 3245, "prof_llm_calls": 19}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:19:40.775451", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_fk7puz", "task_desc": "Send an email to Joana Silva saying something urgent came up and I need to meet her today at 1 PM for 15 minutes. Add that to my calendar and name it “Talk with Joana”. Please tell me when you’ve scheduled the event and sent the email. If she can’t make it, reschedule the event for earliest time that she suggests, as long as I don’t have any other meetings at the same time, and reply to let her know.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Send an email to Joana Silva saying something urgent came up and I need to meet her today at 1 PM for 15 minutes. Add that to my calendar and name it \nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by gathering the information I need: Joana Silva's email address and my current calendar events to avoid conflicts.\nI have Joana's email and my calen\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by finding Joana Silva's email address and checking my calendar for today.\nI found Joana's email and my calendar for today. The 1 PM slot (13:00-13:15) is free. Let me send the email and add the calendar event.\nThe calendar event was created. The email failed because recipients must be a list. Let me retry the email.\nThe email was sent. I received a notification that Joana replied. Let me read her reply to see if she can make it.\nThat's a different email. Let me check the inbox for the new reply from Joana.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me try without the string formatting issue.\nJoana replied: she can't make 1 PM and suggests **1:45 PM or 6 PM** today. Let me check my calendar for conflicts at both times.\n\n- 1:45 PM (13:45-14:00): My events are 09:00-12:00, 18:00-20:00, 20:00-21:00 → free\n- 6 PM (18:00-18:15): I have a Networking Event 18:00-20:00 → conflict!\n\nSo 1:45 PM is the earliest available time. Let me verify there are no other events I might have missed by checking the range, then reschedule.\nConfirmed: 6 PM conflicts with the Networking Event (18:00-20:00). The earliest available time Joana suggested is **1:45 PM**, which is free. Let me reschedule the event and reply to Joana.\nNow let me reply to Joana to confirm 1:45 PM works.\nAll tasks are complete. Let me summarize what I've done.\nThe task is fully complete. Here's what I accomplished:\n\n1. **Sent the email** to Joana Silva (joana.silva@gaia2mail.com) explaining something urgent came up and requesting a 1 PM, 15-minute meeting today.\n\n2. **Added the calendar event** \"Talk with Joana\" for today at 1:00–1:15 PM.\n\n3. **Handled her reply**: Joana couldn't make 1 PM and suggested 1:45 PM or 6 PM. I checked your calendar and found that 6 PM conflicts with your Networking Event (6:00–8:00 PM), while 1:45 PM was free. So I rescheduled the event to the earliest available time she suggested: **today, 1:45–2:00 PM**.\n\n4. **Replied to Joana** confirming 1:45 PM works.\n\nThe event is now scheduled for **1:45 PM today**, and both emails have been sent.\nNo new follow-up message arrived during the wait period. The task is fully complete:\n\n- ✅ Email sent to Joana Silva about the urgent 1 PM meeting request\n- ✅ Calendar event \"Talk with Joana\" created and then rescheduled to 1:45 PM (earliest available time she suggested, since 6 PM conflicted with your Networking Event)\n- ✅ Reply sent to Joana confirming 1:45 PM works\n\nEverything has been handled and there are no pending follow-ups.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2984866f-3766-4daf-a6ea-c774b9e06fc7", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-58c19a37-e8d1-4258-8667-bd0fd5f52c56"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"joana.silva@gaia2mail.com\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Urgent Meeting Request", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Something urgent came up and I need to meet you today at 1 PM for 15 minutes.", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-fde9c444-5bf1-4720-87ff-3776b10c6bb2", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-58c19a37-e8d1-4258-8667-bd0fd5f52c56"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Talk with Joana", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 13:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 13:15:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5fde7c61-d288-4a81-84f2-7e115eb77d33", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-fde9c444-5bf1-4720-87ff-3776b10c6bb2", "OracleEvent-AGENT-2984866f-3766-4daf-a6ea-c774b9e06fc7"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "The event has been scheduled and the email has been sent.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975843.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-efe3d5e7-1d5f-4774-82f6-6ac4ac9f67fb", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-cacebcb0-7ca1-4b15-b8b2-4e91ae9b7692"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "{{OracleEvent-AGENT-fde9c444-5bf1-4720-87ff-3776b10c6bb2}}", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975843.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-39a66ae5-1e78-41cb-ae2e-30f5756fce81", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-cacebcb0-7ca1-4b15-b8b2-4e91ae9b7692"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Talk with Joana", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 13:45:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 14:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975843.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-390743fb-131a-4b2e-b5c9-aee4476adf7a", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-cacebcb0-7ca1-4b15-b8b2-4e91ae9b7692"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "reply_to_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-cacebcb0-7ca1-4b15-b8b2-4e91ae9b7692}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "I have rescheduled the meeting for today at 1:45 PM", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.16666666666666666, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "adaptability", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 502, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.7, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 1225.83, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1225.83, "prof_tok_in": 261195, "prof_tok_out": 1835, "prof_llm_calls": 15}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:20:28.569845", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_isnnos", "task_desc": "Save all available properties that cost less than $1300 if they aren't already saved and email Søren with the total number of newly-saved properties.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Save all available properties that cost less than $1300 if they aren't already saved and email Søren with the total number of newly-saved properties.\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by listing all available apartments to see what's in the catalog.\nThe result was truncated. Let me get the full list by checking the saved apartments\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by listing all available apartments and checking which ones are already saved.\nThe results are truncated. Let me get the full list of all apartments and saved apartments by examining the data more carefully. Let me search for apartments with max_price to find all under $1300, and also get the complete saved list.\nLet me retry with an integer value.\nThe parameter needs to be passed differently. Let me try listing all apartments with a higher limit to get the complete list, and also get the full saved list.\nThe list is being truncated in the display. Let me get the apartment details for the ones I can see and try to find the complete list. The output is being cut off. Let me try the search with a different approach - I'll use the search_apartments with saved_only to understand, but first let me try to get the full list by checking individual apartments. \n\nActually, the issue is the display truncation. Let me try searching with min/max price as the proper type. The error suggests the tool wrapper is converting to string. Let me try without quotes issue - perhaps I need to pass it differently. Let me try the search_apartments with just a location filter to see if it returns complete data.\n\nLet me instead get details on the apartments I can partially see. The truncated one is \"fd4ef3ea31944569b8a9f330bcf51369\" (Lund Living, price 900). Let me get its full details and continue exploring.\nLund Living is already saved (price 900). The list_all_apartments output is truncated, so I need to find all apartments. Let me try the search_apartments tool with max_price as an integer properly. The earlier error was about string type. Let me try passing it as a number without quotes in the value.\nThe search tool has a type issue. Let me work with what I have. The list_all_apartments returns a dict but it's truncated in display. Let me try to get the full picture by listing saved apartments completely and checking each apartment. \n\nLet me get the complete saved list first - it was also truncated. Let me try listing saved apartments again and see if I can get more.\nThe saved list is also truncated. I need to find the complete set of apartments. The list_all_apartments returns a dict keyed by apartment_id. The display truncates. Let me try to enumerate all apartments by getting details on IDs I discover. \n\nThe challenge is finding all apartment IDs. Let me try the search_apartments with a different parameter combination that might work, or try with min_price=0. Actually, the type error happens regardless. \n\nLet me think - the list_all_apartments returns ALL apartments but display truncates. I've seen these IDs so far from both lists:\n- aae6d8011d49417390f7cdc050c4e39a (Östermalm Oasis, 1800, not saved)\n- 835cacdf88584dabb4186d25ecca08ab (Göteborgs Gem, 1200, not saved)\n- 92ba401d76614dc9be065a30c335099c (Malmö Marina, 1500, saved)\n- 0d836a21c18a4e029531ac8ffc9fb3fc (Uppsala Urban, 1000, not saved)\n- fd4ef3ea31944569b8a9f33