{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:21:41.305720", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_d0wx3m", "task_desc": "Please send a Chats message to Akira to let her know that I'm good to attend her birthday party. Notify me once you have sent the message to Akira. When she sets up the calendar invite, please cancel any conflicting events that are scheduled in my calendar at the same time as the event Akira sets up. Book me a premium cab ride to pick me up at home to take me to the address she includes as the event's location. Have the ride pick me up 30 minutes before the party is scheduled. Send a group email", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Please send a Chats message to Akira to let her know that I'm good to attend her birthday party. Notify me once you have sent the message to Akira. Wh\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll work through this task step by step. Let me start by understanding the current state and finding Akira's contact information.\n\nLet me first get the current\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll work through this task step by step. Let me start by understanding the current state and finding Akira's contact information.\nI found Akira. Her Chats user ID is `b6f1ec1a-01b4-4e41-b31a-b3d7a87ecde0`. Let me send the Chats message to her.\nThe message has been sent to Akira. Now let me notify you and then wait for Akira to set up the calendar invite.\nAkira has set up a calendar event. Let me find the event she created to get its details (time and location).\nI found Akira's birthday event:\n- **Title:** Akira's Birthday Bash!!!\n- **Start:** Friday, 2024-10-25 17:00:00\n- **End:** Friday, 2024-10-25 23:00:00\n- **Location:** Regeringsgatan 74, 111 38 Stockholm\n\nNow let me find any conflicting events in my calendar during that time range (2024-10-25 17:00 to 23:00).\nI found two conflicting events (excluding Akira's birthday bash itself):\n1. **Yoga Class** (18:00-19:00) - attendee: Linnea Åström\n2. **Networking Event** (19:00-21:00) - attendees: Linnea Åström, Sunita Bishwakarma\n\nLet me get the full details of these events to confirm attendees before cancelling.\nNow I'll cancel both conflicting events.\nBoth conflicting events are cancelled. The affected people are:\n- **Linnea Åström** (Yoga Class + Networking Event)\n- **Sunita Bishwakarma** (Networking Event)\n\nNow let me book the premium cab ride. The party is at 17:00 on 2024-10-25, so pickup should be 30 minutes before = 16:30. Let me first get a quotation to confirm, then book.\nThe quotation looks good. Now let me book the premium cab ride for pickup at 16:30 on 2024-10-25.\nThe premium cab is booked. Now I need to send a group email to the affected people (Linnea Åström and Sunita Bishwakarma) to apologize and let them know I can't make it. Let me find their email addresses.\nI have both email addresses. Now let me send the group email to the affected people.\nThe recipients need to be a list. Let me retry with the correct format.\nAll tasks are now complete. Let me verify the final state by confirming the conflicting events are gone and the cab is booked.\nEverything is confirmed. All tasks have been completed successfully. Let me provide a final summary.\nAll tasks have been completed successfully:\n\n1. **Chats message to Akira** — Sent letting her know you'll attend her birthday party (and notified you at the time).\n2. **Conflicting events cancelled** — Yoga Class and Networking Event on Oct 25 were deleted after Akira set up her invite.\n3. **Premium cab booked** — Pickup at home at 4:30 PM (30 min before the 5:00 PM party), destination Regeringsgatan 74, 111 38 Stockholm.\n4. **Group apology email** — Sent to Linnea Åström and Sunita Bishwakarma explaining you can't make it.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5a385242-87b9-4bbe-8562-497482c2104f", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-2dd32184-97c1-4dac-8844-a9f904a76f17"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Chats", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "b6f1ec1a-01b4-4e41-b31a-b3d7a87ecde0", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Akira, just confirming that I'm good to attend your birthday party!", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-0e4afd65-f905-4875-a282-e6f269538eb3", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-5a385242-87b9-4bbe-8562-497482c2104f"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "I sent the message to Akira.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975663.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-af79c207-79f5-4c8c-b69a-e5527b8c987d", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-61a632de-20ae-49f3-bfd2-c49292820975"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "b87b0e6f2b1a4f58a19e1bc5d694b315", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975663.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a9ea399c-4bd0-45b3-b475-d03b4b2f67c5", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-61a632de-20ae-49f3-bfd2-c49292820975"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "34a7b40d268c4cad8a36277700628699", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975663.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-04f87b08-166c-43fb-b26e-c3858cf4ce3c", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-61a632de-20ae-49f3-bfd2-c49292820975"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "order_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "start_location", "value": "Home", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_location", "value": "Regeringsgatan 74, 111 38 Stockholm", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "service_type", "value": "Premium", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "ride_time", "value": "2024-10-25 16:30:00", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975663.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-6c4df87e-177c-4a16-8d2d-4d55a8aa9849", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-61a632de-20ae-49f3-bfd2-c49292820975"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"linnea.astrom@gaia2mail.com\",\"sunita.bishwakarma@gaia2mail.com\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Cancellation of Events", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Linnea and Sunita,\n\nUnfortunately, I need to cancel our previously scheduled events due to a conflicting commitment. I apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and appreciate your understanding.\n\nBest regards,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.3333333333333333, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "adaptability", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 510, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 1361.98, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1361.98, "prof_tok_in": 271345, "prof_tok_out": 2216, "prof_llm_calls": 15}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:21:42.713305", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_5fny1x", "task_desc": "Schedule a Networking Prep call for next Monday during the earliest available 1-hour block of time between 10 AM and 2 PM, including all attendees from the Networking Event on that Tuesday. Afterward, send individual Messages or Chats messages to each attendee to notify them about the meeting and confirm their availability for the Networking Event on that Tuesday. I prefer Messages, but if they are not on it, use Chats. Let me know once the meeting has been scheduled and the messages have been s", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Schedule a Networking Prep call for next Monday during the earliest available 1-hour block of time between 10 AM and 2 PM, including all attendees fro\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by understanding the task. Let me break it down:\n\n1. Find the \"Networking Event\" on next Tuesday and get its attendees\n2. Schedule a \"Networking Prep\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by understanding the task. Let me break it down:\n\n1. Find the \"Networking Event\" on next Tuesday and get its attendees\n2. Schedule a \"Networking Prep\" call for next Monday during the earliest available 1-hour block between 10 AM and 2 PM, including all attendees\n3. Send individual Messages/Chats to each attendee to notify them and confirm availability for the Networking Event\n4. Handle any unavailability (replace with Beshoy Gadallah, or cancel event if both unavailable)\n\nLet me first find the Networking Event and check the current date.\nThe current simulation time is around 2024-10-15 (Tuesday). Let me get the full list of Networking Events to find the one on \"next Tuesday\" relative to now. Let me search more specifically.\nI found a Networking Event on Tuesday, 2024-10-15 (today) at 18:00. But the task says \"next Monday\" and \"that Tuesday\" — relative to the current date of 2024-10-15 (Tuesday). So \"next Monday\" would be 2024-10-21, and \"that Tuesday\" would be 2024-10-22.\n\nHowever, the Networking Event on 2024-10-15 is today. Let me check if there's a Networking Event on 2024-10-22 (next Tuesday). The list got cut off. Let me look more carefully at the full range.\nI found the Networking Event on next Tuesday, 2024-10-22, at 19:00-21:00 with attendees:\n- Linnea Åström\n- Sunita Bishwakarma\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Schedule a Networking Prep call for next Monday (2024-10-21) during the earliest available 1-hour block between 10 AM and 2 PM\n2. Check Monday 2024-10-21's existing events to find the earliest available slot\n\nFrom the data I already have for Monday 2024-10-21:\n- Content Creation Session: 10:00-12:00\n- Yoga Class: 18:00-19:00\n\nSo between 10 AM and 2 PM, the 10:00-12:00 block is taken. The earliest available 1-hour block would be 12:00-13:00. Let me verify there are no other events on Monday 2024-10-21 between 10 AM and 2 PM.\nConfirmed. On Monday 2024-10-21, the only events between 10 AM and 2 PM are:\n- Content Creation Session: 10:00-12:00\n\nSo the earliest available 1-hour block between 10 AM and 2 PM is **12:00-13:00**.\n\nNow let me schedule the Networking Prep call for Monday 2024-10-21, 12:00-13:00, with attendees Linnea Åström and Sunita Bishwakarma.\nThe Networking Prep call is scheduled (event_id: d1a1e136f1cff3192730c61913ffb05a).\n\nNow I need to send individual messages to each attendee (Linnea Åström and Sunita Bishwakarma) to notify them about the prep meeting and confirm their availability for the Networking Event on Tuesday 2024-10-22. I prefer Messages, but if they're not on it, use Chats.\n\nLet me first check if these attendees are on Messages (by looking up their user IDs) and Chats.\nResults:\n- **Linnea Åström**: Not found on Messages (empty result), but found on Chats (id: e5e6fd26-a78e-4c9e-92d3-20ec3444b4d0). So I'll use Chats for Linnea.\n- **Sunita Bishwakarma**: Found on Messages (+358936123456), not on Chats. So I'll use Messages for Sunita.\n\nThere are also new message notifications. Let me check those conversations, but first let me send the messages. Actually, let me check the new messages since they may be relevant (possibly from the attendees). Let me read those conversations.\nThese new messages are from a different conversation (about a movie premiere, PTO, etc.) and are not from our two attendees regarding the Networking Event. They're not relevant to this task. The senders are Astrid Svensson and Sunita Bishwakarma, but the content is about other topics, not responses to my prep meeting notification.\n\nNow let me send the messages to the two attendees. I'll use Chats for Linnea Åström and Messages for Sunita Bishwakarma.\nBoth messages have been sent. Now I need to wait for the attendees' responses to confirm their availability for the Networking Event. The task says: \"If any attendee indicates they cannot attend, replace that attendee with Beshoy Gadallah... If both attendees are unavailable, cancel the Networking Event entirely.\"\n\nLet me wait for their responses.\nNo responses yet after 180 seconds. Let me wait a bit longer for the attendees to respond.\nStill no responses. Let me wait a bit more to give the attendees time to reply.\nStill no responses from the attendees. Let me check the conversations directly to see if there are any new messages from Linnea or Sunita regarding the prep meeting/Networking Event.\nThe offset/limit need to be integers. Let me retry.\nThe tool seems to require integer types but the schema passes strings. Let me try reading the specific conversations I already know about to check for new replies. I'll read the Chats con