me do a few more searches to catch any remaining Stockholm apartments, then check crime rates for the expensive ones.\nFound another Stockholm apartment: Östermalms Lyx (2500) - 114 39. Let me do a few more searches to be thorough and catch any remaining Stockholm apartments with different naming patterns.\nI've now done extensive searching. Let me compile the complete list of Stockholm apartments and their prices:\n\n**Stockholm apartments found:**\n1. Stockholm Waterfront - 25000 - 114 56\n2. Stockholm Söder - 22000 - 11825\n3. Södermalm Delight - 18000 - 118 21\n4. Östermalms Lyx - 2500 - 114 39\n5. Stockholm Strand - 2000 - 114 56\n6. Stockholm City Living - 2000 - 111 23\n7. Stockholm Haven - 1800 - 118 26\n8. Östermalm Oasis - 1800 - 114 41\n9. Nordic Oasis - 1800 - 111 35\n10. Södermalm Oasis - 1800 - 118 21\n11. Södermalm Haven - 1800 - 118 25\n\nThe expensive ones (candidates for \"most expensive\") are: **Stockholm Waterfront (25000)**, **Stockholm Söder (22000)**, **Södermalm Delight (18000)**.\n\nNow I need to check the violent crime index for each. Let me get the crime rates for their zip codes. First let me check the API limit, then query the relevant zip codes: 114 56 (Waterfront & Strand), 11825 (Söder), 118 21 (Delight).\nThe three most expensive Stockholm apartments all have violent crime indices ABOVE 25:\n- Stockholm Waterfront (25000): 43.07 ❌\n- Stockholm Söder (22000): 38.08 ❌\n- Södermalm Delight (18000): 29.53 ❌\n\nNone of the top 3 qualify. I need to check the next tier of Stockholm apartments. The remaining Stockholm apartments are all priced at 2500 or below (Östermalms Lyx 2500, Stockholm Strand 2000, Stockholm City Living 2000, and several at 1800). Let me check their crime rates. The zip codes are: 114 39 (Östermalms Lyx), 114 56 (Strand), 111 23 (City Living), 114 41 (Östermalm Oasis), 111 35 (Nordic Oasis), 118 26 (Stockholm Haven), 118 21 (Södermalm Oasis), 118 25 (Södermalm Haven).\n\nI already have 114 56 (43.07) and 118 21 (29.53