a variant made from \"Recycled Paper\" (item_id: faacc5243a374151bf972ccfc1f84bd5, price 39.95, available). This matches \"Ravensburger German Tourists puzzle made from recycled paper.\"\n\nLet me first move the calendar event. I'll delete the old one and create a new one on Oct 18th with the same details.\nNow let me create the event on Oct 18th with the same details.\nThe calendar event has been moved to Oct 18th. Now let me order the puzzle. First, add it to the cart.\nThe cart has the correct item (Ravensburger German Tourists, Recycled Paper). Now let me checkout.\nThe order was placed successfully. Now for the final sub-request: delete my contact from the United States. I need to be careful to identify the correct contact. Let me search for contacts from the United States.\nNo direct matches. Let me list all contacts to find the one from the United States. I'll check both contact apps.\nBoth contact apps appear to share the same data. I see Astrid (Sweden) and Jianhua (China) so far. I need to see all contacts to find one from the United States. Let me get more contacts using offset.\nThe offset parameter requires an integer. Let me try passing it as a number.\nThe tool seems to be receiving the value as a string. Let me try without offset to see if there's a view limit, and check the current user details to understand \"my contact.\"\nThe current user is Astrid Lundqvist (Sweden). The task says \"delete my contact from the United States\" — meaning a contact of the user who is from the United States. I need to find all contacts to locate the US one. The get_contacts with offset is failing due to a type issue. Let me try searching with various US-related terms.\nThe search returns partial matches on various fields but not specifically by country \"United States.\" I need to enumerate all contacts to find the one from the US. The get_contacts offset is failing due to a type issue. Let me try searching with common US city/state names and country terms to surface