{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:28:31.716558", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_73o3ij", "task_desc": "I have a brand partnership meeting with Åke Svensson on zoom on Saturday 10/19/2024 from 2 pm - 4 pm. Switch that to an in-person meeting at the office, Stortorget 13, 211 22 Malmö, and then send an email to Åke letting him know the change. In the email also send Åke the article labeled metro_herald 740 and ask him to review it before the meeting. After sending the email, order one pack of the Painting Panel Canvas Boards for the meeting. Let me know if you are unsure about anything, I can't aff", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: I have a brand partnership meeting with Åke Svensson on zoom on Saturday 10/19/2024 from 2 pm - 4 pm. Switch that to an in-person meeting at the offic\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by examining the calendar event for the meeting with Åke Svensson, and look up the contact and article details.\nThe search didn't show the specific S\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by gathering the information I need: the calendar event, Åke Svensson's contact details, and the article labeled metro_herald 740.\nI found Åke's contact. The search results didn't show the specific meeting yet. Let me search more specifically and look for the article file.\nI found the meeting event (event_id: f041377cce14424692cf96b15fc4fd0b). Now I need to find the article labeled \"metro_herald 740\". Let me search the Documents folder.\nFound the article at `/Documents/news/metro_herald_740.txt`. Let me read it to understand its content so I can reference it in the email.\nThe file appears to be empty or unreadable as text. Let me try reading it as a document.\nThe article file is empty. This is something I should flag to the user, but I can still attach the file to the email as requested. Let me first update the calendar event to be in-person at the office, then proceed.\n\nLet me update the calendar event location and description.\nNow let me update the event to be in-person at the office. I'll change the location and update the description to note it's now in-person.\nI've created the updated in-person event. Now let me delete the old Zoom event to avoid a duplicate.\nNow let me send the email to Åke. I'll attach the article file and let him know about the change.\nThe recipients parameter needs to be a list. Let me retry.\nThe email was sent successfully. Now let me order one pack of the Painting Panel Canvas Boards. Let me find the product first.\nThe product is \"Horizon Group USA Painting Panel Canvas Boards, 9x12, Pack of 12\" (product_id: c1131c0e691eb6bced30c8bb4d83d6bd). The task says \"one pack\" — the product is sold as a pack of 12. I'll add one unit (one pack) to the cart. Let me add it using the default variant item_id.\nThe quantity needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nThe tool seems to be receiving the value as a string. Let me try without specifying quantity (default is 1).\nThe item was added to the cart. Let me verify the cart contents and then checkout.\nThe cart has one pack of the Painting Panel Canvas Boards. Now let me checkout.\nThe order was placed successfully. Let me verify the order details.\nAll tasks are complete. Let me summarize what I did and flag the one issue I encountered.\n\nHere's a summary of everything I completed for your meeting with Åke Svensson:\n\n**1. Calendar update ✅**\n- Found the original Zoom meeting (Sat, Oct 19, 2024, 2:00–4:00 pm) and switched it to an in-person meeting.\n- New event: **Brand Partnership Meeting** at **Stortorget 13, 211 22 Malmö**, same date/time, attendee Åke Svensson. The old Zoom event was deleted to avoid a duplicate.\n\n**2. Email to Åke ✅**\n- Sent to ake.svensson@dif.se with the subject \"Brand Partnership Meeting - Change to In-Person at Our Malmö Office.\"\n- The email explains the switch from Zoom to in-person at the office, and attaches the article **metro_herald 740**, asking him to review it before the meeting.\n\n**3. Order placed ✅**\n- Ordered **1 pack** of \"Horizon Group USA Painting Panel Canvas Boards, 9x12, Pack of 12\" (Cotton, Medium, Textured). Order ID `c876c5115bad4b728e68316a0895a2aa`, total $14.99, status: processed.\n\n**⚠️ One thing to flag (please double-check):**\n- The article file `/Documents/news/metro_herald_740.txt` is **empty** — it contains no text content. I still attached it to the email as you requested, but Åke won't be able to review any actual content from it. You may want to locate the correct article file and resend, or send it to him separately.\n- Also, I used the email address **ake.svensson@dif.se** from Åke's contact record. Please confirm that's the right address for him.\n\nLet me know if you'd like me to correct either of those.\nAll task components have been completed via tool calls. Let me deliver the final summary to the user.\nI've delivered the final summary to you. All parts of the task are complete:\n\n1. **Calendar** — Switched the meeting from Zoom to in-person at Stortorget 13, 211 22 Malmö (Sat Oct 19, 2–4 pm), and removed the old Zoom event.\n2. **Email** — Sent to Åke (ake.svensson@dif.se) notifying him of the change and attaching the metro_herald 740 article for review.\n3. **Order** — Placed for 1 pack of Painting Panel Canvas Boards (order c876c5115bad4b728e68316a0895a2aa, $14.99, processed).\n\nTwo items I flagged for your verification: the metro_herald_740 file is empty (so Åke has nothing to actually review), and the email address came from Åke's contact record — please confirm both are correct.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-98ac3a02-03b4-42d4-a161-7ce1b6a9a2eb", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-2b5d59e5-d488-4c5a-8048-45186214502d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "f041377cce14424692cf96b15fc4fd0b", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1703da6f-cc98-47e3-be72-713a593e36a7", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-2b5d59e5-d488-4c5a-8048-45186214502d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Brand Partnership Meeting", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 14:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 16:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "Work", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "Discuss brand partnership details and expectations.", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "office, Stortorget 13, 211 22 Malmö", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Åke Svensson\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-59a9e41f-a613-4bbb-80fa-86cfaaa5bcf6", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-1703da6f-cc98-47e3-be72-713a593e36a7"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"ake.svensson@dif.se\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Update on Brand Partnership Meeting", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hi Åke,\n\nI've changed the location of our meeting on Saturday 10/19/2024 to the office at Stortorget 13, 211 22 Malmö. I've attached an article (metro_herald_740.txt) for you to review before our meeting.\n\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[\"/Documents/news/metro_herald_740.txt\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-dd3cd8e3-dbd5-44cb-9da5-987fb2508007", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-59a9e41f-a613-4bbb-80fa-86cfaaa5bcf6"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Which Painting Panel Canvas Boards option would you like to order?", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.25, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "ambiguity", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 530, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.7, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 1280.86, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1280.86, "prof_tok_in": 374474, "prof_tok_out": 2815, "prof_llm_calls": 20}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:28:31.717108", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_2edv2p", "task_desc": "I dislike the current campaign I'm promoting, so please, delete all events tagged as work in my calendar starting tomorrow through this Saturday, send a message to the most frequent attendee of those events on Chats saying \"Get me out of this deal, fast!\" and email my Swedish marketing manager to let them know I need a new brand deal. If I don't email this person, I might get fired.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: I dislike the current campaign I'm promoting, so please, delete all events tagged as work in my calendar starting tomorrow through this Saturday, send\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Find all calendar events tagged \"work\" from tomorrow (2024-10-16) through Saturday (2024-10-19), and delete them.\n2. \nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Find all calendar events tagged \"work\" from tomorrow (2024-10-16) through Saturday (2024-10-19), and delete them.\n2. Identify the most frequent attendee across those events.\n3. Send a Chats message to that attendee saying \"Get me out of this deal, fast!\"\n4. Find my Swedish marketing manager contact and email them about needing a new brand deal.\n\nLet me start by getting the work-tagged events and the current time.\nThe tag query returned empty. Let me verify by checking all tags and listing events in the date range directly.\nThe tag is \"Work\" (capitalized). Let me query with the correct casing and also list events in the date range.\nThe tag query works with \"Work\". The events returned are from August, not in my target range. Let me get the full list of Work events to see all of them, and fix the date-range query with integer types.\nThe date-range query keeps erroring on the integer type. Let me try without offset/limit parameters (using defaults) to get events in the target range.\nThe date-range query works without offset/limit. I can see Work events in the target range. Let me get the full list of events in the range to identify all Work-tagged ones. Let me read more events.\nThe offset/limit parameters must be passed as actual integers, not strings. Let me try with integer values.\nThe tool seems to reject string-typed integers. Let me try the default call again to get the next page of events (it returned 5 events last time, default limit is 10). Let me call without offset/limit to see if it paginates differently, and also try a different approach by searching events.\n\nActually, the first call returned 5 events with default limit 10. Let me try calling again - perhaps it returns the same. Instead, let me search for Work events in the range by using the tag list and cross-referencing. But the tag list returned August events only (it seems to return all Work events regardless of date). Let me re-examine - the tag query returned events but got truncated. Let me get the full Work events list to find all of them, then filter by date range.\n\nLet me call get_calendar_events_by_tag again and look at the complete result.\nThe tag query result is being truncated in display. I need to identify all Work events in the Oct 16-19 range. The date-range query is the reliable way. Let me try the date-range query with integer offset/limit passed differently. Since string fails, let me try without those params but the default returned only 5 events. \n\nLet me try calling the date-range query again - maybe it returns more events on a fresh call, or maybe I need to page. Let me try with limit only.\nThe tool strictly requires integer types which the harness passes as strings. The default call (no offset/limit) returned 5 events. Let me call it again to see if it returns the next set or the same set.\nThe result is truncated at the same point (5 events shown, then \"Cont...\"). The display truncates but the actual data may be complete. Let me try to get the full data by reading individual events. First, I have 3 confirmed Work events on Oct 16. I need to find Work events on Oct 17, 18, 19 too.\n\nLet me narrow the date range to each day to get complete results per day. Let me query Oct 17-19 range.\nNow I can see Oct 17 Work events. The display truncates but I'm getting the data. Let me continue with Oct 18-19 range.\nNow I have the Oct 18-19 events. Let me also get the complete Oct 16 and Oct 17 lists with their totals. Let me re-query Oct 16 and Oct 17 with narrower ranges to capture all events and their totals.\nNow I have a complete picture. Let me compile the Work-tagged events from Oct 16 (tomorrow) through Oct 19 (Saturday):\n\n**Oct 16 (Wed):**\n- 81141f54d8904d15b58faaff860d0d65 - Brand Partnership Meeting (Work) - attendee: Åke Svensson\n- 7491df4dfb5d4586b3d43c0f4f9e81d5 - Content Creation Session (Work) - no attendees\n- 15a8031c0f1e4e6c867b93b08a5d365b - Social Media Management (Work) - no attendees\n\n**Oct 17 (Thu):**\n- 2c50e300723342fd890a082b5b19cbba - Content Creation Session (Work) - no attendees\n- 06551b52bea4471a87591728dfb818ab - Social Media Management (Work) - no attendees\n- 4ef002bd4c244d74a176d172b6d3094a - Brand Partnership Meeting (Work) - attendee: Åke Svensson\n\n**Oct 18 (Fri):**\n- 1b1df251b5044fab93d395277aff298a - Content Creation Session (Work) - no attendees\n\n**Oct 19 (Sat):**\n- f041377cce14424692cf96b15fc4fd0b - Brand Partnership Meeting (Work) - attendee: Åke Svensson\n\n**Most frequent attendee:** Åke Svensson (appears in 3 events: Oct 16, 17, 19). All other events have no attendees.\n\nNow let me delete all 10 Work events and find the Swedish marketing manager. Let me first look up the attendee's chat user id and search for the Swedish marketing manager contact.\nAll 8 Work events deleted (the 2 remaining Oct 16/17 events were Health/Personal, correctly left). Åke Svensson's chat user id is `dd868d91-a65d-43bc-ab1a-3090c6932f4f`. The contact search for \"marketing manager\" returned nothing. Let me search contacts more broadly to find the Swedish marketing manager.\nFound it. **Astrid Svensson** (contact_id: a94c913d707d4c308f086cba42165741) is a Swedish Marketing Manager. Let me get her full contact details to find her email address.\nAstrid Svensson's email is `astrid.svensson@gaia2mail.com`. Now let me send the Chat message to Åke Svensson and the email to Astrid Svensson.\nThe chat message was sent. The email failed because recipients must be a list. Let me retry with a list.\nAll sub-tasks are now complete. Let me verify the deletions took effect by checking the date range once more.\nAll Work events have been deleted — only the Health (Yoga) and Personal events remain in the Oct 16–19 range. All three sub-tasks are complete.\nTask complete. I deleted all 8 Work-tagged calendar events from tomorrow (Oct 16) through Saturday (Oct 19), sent the Chat message \"Get me out of this deal, fast!\" to Åke Svensson (the most frequent attendee of those events, appearing in all 3 Brand Partnership Meetings), and emailed your Swedish marketing manager Astrid Svensson to request a new brand deal.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1b8058da-f492-4cce-8f07-ae3f509859de", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-7762adbb-7467-44f5-a40e-37fc8048269f"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "81141f54d8904d15b58faaff860d0d65", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-e4c15bb