inatas and 1 of the most expensive candy filling pinatas have been ordered.\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.375, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "adaptability", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 630, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "5c172812", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "eaae534dbfcc", "prof_total_s": 1390.63, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1390.63, "prof_tok_in": 784032, "prof_tok_out": 4825, "prof_llm_calls": 40}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T11:38:30.669167", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_gjw61a", "task_desc": "Schedule a Property Tour event at the most expensive 4 bedroom property in my saved list for this Saturday from 4pm - 5pm. Add the participants of the the most recently updated Messages conversation 'Catching up with friends' as attendees (besides me). Book me a premium cab from Stora Södergatan 25, Lund to the property location (including the zip code) one hour before the property tour starts. Send each of the attendees separate Messages messages with the time and place of the tour. If a new fu", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Schedule a Property Tour event at the most expensive 4 bedroom property in my saved list for this Saturday from 4pm - 5pm. Add the participants of the\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Find the most expensive 4-bedroom property in my saved list\n2. Find the most recently updated Messages conversation '\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Find the most expensive 4-bedroom property in my saved list\n2. Find the most recently updated Messages conversation 'Catching up with friends' and its participants\n3. Schedule a Property Tour event this Saturday 4pm-5pm at that property\n4. Book a premium cab from Stora Södergatan 25, Lund to the property location one hour before\n5. Send each attendee a separate Messages message with time and place\n6. Monitor for 3 minutes for a new furnished 4-bedroom property in same zip code that's more expensive; if found, move everything and notify attendees\n\nLet me start by gathering the needed information.\nThe saved apartments list was truncated. Let me get the full list and also check the conversation details. Let me search for 4-bedroom saved apartments specifically and read the conversation.\nThe search needs an int. Let me fix that. Also, I need to verify which conversation is titled 'Catching up with friends' and find the most recently updated one. Let me search with int and check conversation titles.\nThe tools require int types, not strings. Let me retry with proper int values.\nThe parameter serialization is treating my values as strings. Let me try passing them as bare numbers without quotes in the value.\nThe tool keeps receiving a string. Let me try a different approach - list all saved apartments fully to find 4-bedroom ones, and list recent conversations with integer values. Let me try the list functions which may be more lenient.\nThe list_saved_apartments returns truncated results. The search_apartments and list_recent_conversations tools are rejecting my int parameters. Let me try the search_apartments with the parameter passed differently, and try reading the conversation that matched the search to confirm its title. First, let me check the conversation titles by reading a few of the matched ones. But I need to confirm which is 'Catching up with friends'. Let me try the search_apartments tool again with a different format and also try list_recent_conversations.\n\nActually, the issue is the JSON serialization. Let me try passing the integer without it being interpreted as string by using the bare number format.\nThe search_apartments tool consistently rejects the int. Let me work with what I have. I'll get the full saved apartments list by reading it in detail, and identify 4-bedroom ones. The list was truncated at \"8fb973f7cd694f589755f5755a0dd8ba\". Let me get apartment details for that one and continue. But first, I need a complete list. Let me try the search with saved_only only (no bedrooms filter) to get all saved, then filter manually.\nThe boolean is also being passed as string. The serialization layer is converting all values to strings. Let me try the list_recent_conversations with integer values once more, perhaps the issue is intermittent. Actually, let me try a completely different approach and just read the conversation that matched the search to find its title, and get apartment details for the truncated one.\n\nLet me read the remaining saved apartments by getting details on the truncated ID, and also read the other matched conversations to find 'Catching up with friends'.\nI have two saved apartments so far with 4 bedrooms not yet found. The list is truncated. I need the complete saved list. The search_apartments tool rejects int/bool params. Let me try list_all_apartments to see the full catalog and cross-reference with saved ones, but that won't tell me which are saved. \n\nBetter approach: the list_saved_apartments returns a dict that gets truncated in display. Let me try to get the rest by checking the remaining IDs. But I don't know all IDs. Let me try list_all_apartments to understand the catalog, and separately try to get the full saved list.\n\nActually, let me retry the search_apartments with proper types - maybe I need to not quote. The error persists. Let me try list_all_apartments first.\nThe list_all_apartments also truncates. I need a reliable way to get the full saved list. The search_apartments tool rejects my int/bool. Let me try once more with the exact parameter format - perhaps the issue is that I must pass the value as a JSON number. Let me try with the bare number format that the system expects.\nThe search_apartments tool consistently fails. Let me work around it. I'll get the full saved list by paginating through list_all_apartments and filtering for saved=true, since the saved list display truncates. But that's also truncated. \n\nAlternative: I can identify 4-bedroom saved apartments by checking each saved apartment's details. I have IDs from the saved list so far:\n- 62cb7292b5a54171a312e34ff332356d (Helsingborg Haven, 3br)\n- d8f02d5d11c14e5588120a316cbafef4 (Uppsala Studentboende, 1br)\n- 256aeabd73374a37ba8f0bb64386ba6e (Jönköping Jewel, 3br)\n- 49c463a034404ca4a48bfbf5353a9021 (Lund Botaniska, 2br)\n- 8fb973f7cd694f589755f5755a0dd8ba (Uppsala Oasis, 2br)\n\nThere are more saved apartments truncated. I need to find them. Let me try list_all_apartments with offset to get the rest, and identify saved ones. Let me get the next page.\nThe list_all_apartments doesn't support offset and returns the same truncated view. I need the complete saved list. The search_apartments tool is the right tool but rejects int. Let me try passing the parameter as a JSON number without the string wrapper by using a different representation. \n\nActually, the issue might be that the harness wraps everything in strings. Let me try the search_apartments with number_of_bedrooms as a value that might parse. Let me try once more but this is clearly a serialization issue on my end. \n\nLet me instead try to get the full saved list by reading each apartment. I'll need to discover all saved IDs. From the saved list, I have 5 IDs and it truncated mid-6th. Let me try list_saved_apartments again - maybe it returns the same but I can see if there's a pattern. \n\nActually, a better approach: the search tool might work if I only pass number_of_bedrooms. Let me try just that one parameter.\nThe search_apartments tool is unusable due to the int serialization issue. I'll work with the saved list directly. I have 5 saved apartment IDs and the list truncated at a 6th. Let me get the full saved list by trying list_saved_apartments - it may return all but display truncates. \n\nLet me think: I need to find ALL 4-bedroom saved apartments. The saved list returned 5 complete + 1 partial. Let me try to retrieve more saved apartments by checking if there's a way. Since list_saved_apartments returns a dict (all at once), and it's truncated in display, I cannot see beyond. \n\nLet me try the search_apartments one more time but with the value formatted as a number. Perhaps the harness needs me to write it differently. I'll attempt with no quotes around the number.\nThe search_apartments tool is fundamentally broken for me due to type serialization. I'll proceed by enumerating saved apartments manually. I have these saved IDs from the list:\n1. 62cb7292b5a54171a312e34ff332356d - Helsingborg Haven (3br)\n2. d8f02d5d11c14e5588120a316cbafef4 - Uppsala Studentboende (1br)\n3. 256aeabd73374a37ba8f0bb64386ba6e - Jönköping Jewel (3br)\n4. 49c463a034404ca4a48bfbf5353a9021 - Lund Botaniska (2br)\n5. 8fb973f7cd694f589755f5755a0dd8ba - Uppsala Oasis (2br)\n6. (truncated - need to find)\n\nI need to find the 6th+ saved apartments. Let me get details on the truncated one. The truncation happened right after \"8fb973f7cd694f589755f5755a0dd8ba\": {\"name\": \"Uppsala Oasis\"...}. The next apartment ID wasn't shown. \n\nLet me try list_all_apartments to find saved ones I haven't seen, by scanning the full catalog. But it's also truncated. However, I can identify saved apartments from the catalog by their saved=true flag. Let me look at what I've seen in list_all: 92ba401d76614dc9be065a30c335099c (Malmö Marina, saved=true). That's a 6th saved apartment! Let me get its details and continue scanning the catalog for more saved ones.\n\nLet me get details on Malmö Marina and also try t", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-8e4fcf55-b253-4826-a081-834aa43ca375", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-df17e0e3-7061-4137-8c72-3460f5a7f280"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Property Tour", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 16:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 17:00